hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3001","3 - Chapter on the right of a Muslim over a Muslim. 2524/1 - Musaddad said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us. 2524/2 - And Ishaq said: Abdillah ibn Yazid al-Muqri and Yala ibn Ubayd informed us, saying: al-Ifriqi Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn Anum narrated to us, saying: I heard my father say: He gathered them at their anchorages during their naval expedition, at the vessel of Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him. He said: When our lunch arrived, we sent for Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, and the people of his vessel, so Abu Ayyub came to us and said: You invited me while I am fasting, and it was my duty to answer you. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A Muslim has six obligatory traits over a Muslim; whoever abandons one of them abandons an obligatory right of his brother upon him: to answer him when he invites him, to greet him when he meets him, to say yarhamuk Allah when he sneezes, to visit him when he is ill, to follow his funeral when he dies, and to advise him when he seeks his advice. The wording is Musaddad's. This is a hasan hadith, and it has a witness in Sahih Muslim from the hadith of Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him."
"3002","2524/3 - Al-Harith said: Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us with it similarly, and he mentioned the hadith, saying: Among us was a jesting man and a man in charge of our expenses."
"3003","2524/4 - And Ahmad ibn Mani said: Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman, from his father, who said: We raided by sea with Muawiyah, may Allah be pleased with him, and our vessel joined a vessel containing Abu Ayyub, may Allah be pleased with him. When our lunch arrived, we sent for him and he came to us, and he mentioned the hadith, saying: With us was a jesting man who would say to the keeper of our food: O so-and-so, may Allah reward you with good and evil. When he persisted, he would anger him and insult him. The jester said: What do you say, O Abu Ayyub, if I say: May Allah reward you with good and evil, and he insults me? Abu Ayyub said: You said to him, for we used to say: Whomsoever good does not reform, evil will reform. The jester said to the man: May Allah reward you with evil and mange. He laughed and was pleased, saying: Do not abandon your idleness in any case. The jester said: May Allah reward Abu Ayyub with good, for he told me."
"3004","2525/1 - Ishaq said: al-Walid ibn Muslim informed us, from al-Awzai, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit the weak among the Muslims, visit their sick, and attend their funerals."
"3005","2525/2 - Ishaq said: And it was mentioned to us from Sufyan ibn Husayn that he used to mention, meaning from al-Zuhri, from Abu Umamah, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly. I say: The route of Sufyan ibn Husayn was narrated with a chain by Abu Yala and al-Tabarani, and there is weakness in Sufyan's narration from al-Zuhri, but it is strengthened by al-Walid's narration from al-Awzai."
"3006","2526 - Ishaq said: Ararah ibn al-Birind informed us, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever aids his Muslim brother in his absence, Allah will aid him in this world and the Hereafter; and whoever conceals his Muslim brother, Allah will conceal him in this world and the Hereafter."
"3007","2527 - Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid informed us, Yahya ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever honors his Muslim brother honors Allah Almighty."
"3008","2528 - Ahmad said in al-Zuhd: Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, who said: They used to say: The Muslim is the mirror of his brother, showing him of himself what he does not see."
"3009","2529 - Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdillah informed us, Mamar informed me, from Yahya ibn al-Mukhtar, from al-Hasan, who said: The believer is a part of the believer, at his service for his need; he must take pains for him, rejoice at his joy and grieve at his grief. He is the mirror of his brother: if he sees in him what displeases him, he corrects him, straightens him, directs him, and disputes with him in private and in public."
"3010","2530/1 - Ahmad ibn Mani said: Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibrahim, freedman of Banu Hashim, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and squatted before him, saying: O Messenger of Allah, teach me, for I am a coarse Bedouin. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Fear Allah, and do not belittle any good deed, even pouring from your vessel into your companion's vessel, and even meeting your brother with a cheerful face... the hadith."
"3011","2530/2 - Abu Yala said: Surayj, that is Ibn Yunus, narrated to us, Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us with this, adding: And if a man reviles you and reproaches you with what he knows of you, do not reproach him with what you know of him, for its evil consequence will be upon him and its reward for you."
"3012","4 - Chapter on kindness to parents. 2531/1 - Musaddad said: Ismail, that is Ibn Ulayyah, narrated to us. 2531/2 - And Ishaq said: Ibn Ulayyah informed us, from Ziyad ibn Mikhraq, from Taysalah ibn Mayyas, who said: I was with the Najdat... and he mentioned the hadith. He said: When Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, saw my fear, he said: Do you fear entering the Fire? I said: Yes. He said: Do you love to enter Paradise? I said: Yes. He said: Are your parents alive? I said: I have my mother with me. He said: By Allah, if you speak gently to her and feed her, you will surely enter Paradise, so long as you avoid the mortal sins."
"3013","2532 - Abd said: Umar ibn Said al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Said ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Tanukhi narrated to us, from Makhul, from Umm Ayman, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: She heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advising one of his family, saying: Obey your parents, even if they command you to give up your property... the hadith. 2533/1 - Umar narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from al-Zuhri: the one advised with this counsel was Thawban, may Allah be pleased with him."
"3014","2533/2 - Abu Yala said: Abu Bakr ibn Zanjawayh narrated to us, Abu Mushir narrated to us, Said ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us... the hadith."
"3015","2534 - Al-Tayalisi said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Adi ibn Adi, from his father, who said: Umar said: We used to recite among what is recited: Do not turn away from your fathers, for it is disbelief in you."
"3016","2535 - Musaddad said: Hushaym narrated to us, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, who said: I said to Mujahid: The prayer is established while my father calls me? He said: Answer your father."
"3017","2536 - And Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, from Makhul, who said: If your mother calls you while you are in prayer, answer her; but if your father calls you, do not answer him until you finish."
"3018","2537/1 - Ibn Abi Umar said: al-Hakam ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Abd al-Quddus ibn Habib al-Dimashqi narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim who wakes in the morning with his parents pleased with him except that he has two doors to Paradise; if only one, then one. And there is no Muslim who wakes in the morning with his parents angry with him except that he has two doors to the Fire; if only one, then one."
"3019","2537/2 - Abu Yala said: Zuhayr narrated to us, Shababab narrated to us, al-Mughirah, that is Ibn Muslim, narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and he mentioned it, adding at its end: A man, I think, said: O Messenger of Allah, even if they wronged him? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Even if they wronged him, even if they wronged him, even if they wronged him, three times. The chain of Abu Yala is hasan, and it was also narrated mawquf (stopped)."
"3020","2537/3 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Sad ibn Masud, who said: I said to Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: I am a man keen on jihad, and none of my people remains except that he has joined the garrison towns or jihad, except my parents, or he said: except my family and my parents, or he said: my father dislikes that. He looked at me and said: No man has two parents and wakes doing good to them except that a door to Paradise is opened for him; and he does not reach evening doing good except that two doors of Paradise are opened for him. He said: I said: Doing good to them? He said: Yes; if there is only one and he wakes doing good, a door of Paradise is opened for him. And neither of them nor one of them is angry with him without Allah being pleased with him until he is pleased. I said: Even if he wronged him? He said: Even if he wronged him."
"3021","2538 - Ibn Abi Umar said: Waki narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from a man of the Ansar: that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My father seized my wealth from me. He said: You and your wealth belong to your father."
"3022","2539 - Ahmad ibn Mani said: Hammad narrated to us, from al-Kalbi, from Abu Salih, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah Almighty increases a man's lifespan through his kindness to his parents. Al-Kalbi is abandoned (matruk)."
"3023","2540 - Ibn Mani also said: Hushaym narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended the pulpit one day; when he placed his foot on the lowest step he said: Amin; then he placed his foot (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the second and said: Amin; then he placed his foot (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the third step and said: Amin. When he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his sermon and descended, they said: O Messenger of Allah, you did such-and-such? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me when I placed my foot on the lowest step and said: O Muhammad, whoever reaches his parents or one of them and is not forgiven, then dies and enters the Fire, may Allah distance him; say: Amin. So I said: Amin... the hadith."
"3024","2541/1 - Hushaym narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ubaydillah narrated to us, from his father: that he heard Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly."
"3025","2541/2 - Abu Yala said: Abu Mamar al-Hilali narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, similarly."
"3026","2542 - Abd ibn Humayd said: Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Dirghamah ibn Ulaybah ibn Harmalah, from his father, from his grandfather, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and prayed with him. When he finished the prayer, he looked at the faces of the people, hardly distinguishing their faces after the prayer was finished; when it drew near, he departed. I said: O Messenger of Allah, advise me... and he mentioned the hadith. And his father Ulaybah was dutiful to his father Harmalah: when at home, he would look for the softest spot and seat him in it, and look for the fullest, tastiest bone and give it to him; and when traveling, he would look for the gentlest camel among his mounts and carry him on it; such was his devotion to him."
"3027","2543 - Al-Harith said: al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, from Munir ibn al-Zubayr: that he heard Makhul saying: Kindness to parents expiates major sins, and a man remains able to do good so long as there remains among his kin one older than him. This is mawquf, and its narrator from Makhul is weak."
"3028","2544 - Al-Harith also said: Awn ibn Umarah narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from al-Hasan, who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, whom shall I honor most? He said: Your mother. He said: Then whom? He said: Your mother. He said: Then whom? He said: Then your father. He said: Then whom? He said: The nearest, then the nearest."
"3029","2545 - Said ibn Amir narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, saying: al-Hudhayl ibn Hafsah used to gather firewood in summer and peel it, and take reeds and split them. Hafsah said: I would feel cold, so he would bring the brazier and place it behind me while I prayed, though he had others who could suffice him if he wished; he would kindle for me that peeled firewood and split reeds as fuel to warm me without the heat harming me. She said: Sometimes I wanted to turn to him and say: O my son, return to your family, then I would remember what he intended and leave him. He would go on raids and pilgrimage; he caught a fever when the Hajj season arrived, then recovered, and before I knew it he had entered ihram for Hajj. I said: O my son, it is as if you feared I would prevent you; I would not have done so. She said: He had a milch she-camel and would send me morning milk, and I would say: O my son, you know I do not drink it while fasting. He would say: O mother of al-Hudhayl, the tastiest milk is what stays overnight in the camel's udder; give it to whomever you wish to drink. She said: When he died, Allah Almighty granted patience as He willed, except that I felt a choking grief that would not go away. While I was praying one night reciting Surah al-Nahl until I came to this verse: Do not exchange the covenant of Allah for a small price; what is with Allah is better for you if you only knew. What is with you perishes, and what is with Allah remains; and We will surely reward those who were patient with their reward according to the best of what they used to do. She said: I repeated it, and Allah removed what I felt."
"3030","2546 - Abu Yala said: Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Harb al-Hilali narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ishaq ibn Dajah al-Madani narrated to me, Iqal ibn Shabih ibn Iqal ibn Sasah al-Mujashii narrated to me, my father narrated to me, from my grandfather, from his father Sasah, who said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, whom shall I honor most? He said: Your mother, your father, your sister, your brother, the nearest, the nearest."
"3031","2547 - Hudbah narrated to us, Hazm ibn Abi Hazm al-Qutai narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Burdah, that is Ibn Abi Musa, who said: I came to Madinah, and Abdillah ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, came to me and said to me: Do you know why I came to you? I said: No. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever loves to maintain ties with his father in his grave, let him maintain his father's brothers after him. And there was brotherhood and affection between my father Umar and your father, so I loved to maintain that. Ibn Hibban narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Hudbah, with it."
"3032","2548 - Abu Yala also said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Maymun ibn Najih narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I desire jihad but cannot do it. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is any of your parents still alive? He said: My mother. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Devote yourself to Allah in kindness to her; if you do that, you are a pilgrim, an umrah performer, and a warrior when your mother is pleased with you; so fear Allah and be dutiful to her."
"3033","2549 - Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to me, from Zabban ibn Faid, from Sahl ibn Muadh, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is dutiful to his parents, glad tidings to him, and Allah will increase his lifespan. Zabban is weak."
"3034","2550 - Abu Hammam narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Naim, freedman of Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, set out for Hajj until, between Makkah and Madinah, he came to a tree he recognized and sat beneath it, then said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) beneath a tree when a young man came from these mountain paths until he stood before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have come to strive with you in the path of Allah Almighty, seeking thereby the face of Allah Almighty and the Hereafter. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Are both your parents alive? He said: Yes. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then go out and be dutiful to them. He said: So he turned back from where he came."
"3035","2551 - Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah said: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Kathir ibn Abdillah narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: I was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he said: The ally of a people is one of them, and the son of a people's sister is one of them."
"3036","5 - Chapter on the prohibition of attributing oneself to other than one's patrons, claiming descent from other than one's fathers, and reviling parents. 2552 - Abu Yala said: Amr ibn al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, Mutarrif narrated to us, from Talhah, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever claims descent from other than his father, or attaches himself to other than his patrons out of aversion to them, upon him is the curse of Allah; and whoever reviles his father or his parents, likewise."
"3037","2553 - Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Abu Hafs al-Abbar narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had two freedmen, an Abyssinian and a Nabatean; they reviled each other while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) listened. One of them said to his companion: O Abyssinian, and the other said: O Nabatean. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not say this; you are both but two men from among the Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3038","6 - Chapter on the virtue of one blessed with daughters who is patient with them. 2554 - Ahmad ibn Mani said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, from Ibn Hudayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is blessed with a female child and does not bury her alive, humiliate her, or prefer his male child over her, Allah Almighty will admit him to Paradise through her."
"3039","2555/1 - And Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Fitr narrated to us, from Shurahbil ibn Sad, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is blessed with two daughters and treats them well as long as they accompany him, Allah Almighty will admit him to Paradise through them."
"3040","2555/2 - Abu Yala said: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Fitr with it."
"3041","2556/1 - Musaddad said: Khalid narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Qays, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever shelters an orphan from among the Muslims to his food and drink until he satisfies him, Paradise becomes due for him, unless he commits a sin that is not forgiven; and whoever maintains three daughters, disciplines them and treats them well, Paradise becomes due for him. They said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or two daughters? He said: Or two daughters; so much so that had they said: one, he would have said: one. And whoever loses his two precious ones, his reward with Allah is Paradise. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what are his two precious ones? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: His two eyes. And when Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated this hadith, he would say: This is among the choicest and finest of hadith."
"3042","2556/2 - Abd ibn Humayd said: Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us with it."
"3043","2556/3 - Al-Harith said: Ubaydillah ibn Umar narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, from his father, from Hanash, that is Husayn ibn Qays, with it."
"3044","2556/4 - Abu Yala said: Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us with it."
"3045","7 - Chapter on the virtue of kindness to the orphan. 2557/1 - Abu Bakr said: Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, Safwan ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Umm Said bint Amr ibn Murrah al-Jumahi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sponsors an orphan, his own or another's, I and he will be in Paradise like these two fingers, the middle one and the glorifying one next to it."
"3046","2557/2 - Abu Ya'la said: Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us with it. Thus Muhammad ibn Amr narrated it, and Sufyan differed from him, from Safwan."
"3047","2558/1 - Al-Humaydi said: Sufyan narrated to us, Safwan ibn Sulaym narrated to me, from a woman called Unaysah, from Umm Said bint Murrah al-Fihri, from her father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I and the guardian of the orphan, for him or for another, will be in Paradise like these two, and Sufyan pointed with his two fingers."
"3048","2558/2 - Al-Harith said: Al-Humaydi Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us with this. 2558/3 - Musaddad said: Sufyan narrated to us with this, and added: if he fears Allah, mighty and majestic."
"3049","2559 - Al-Humaydi said: Sufyan narrated to us, Ismail ibn Umayyah narrated to us, saying: I was informed that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I and the guardian of the orphan, for him or for another, will be in Paradise, when he fears Allah Almighty, like these two, and Al-Humaydi pointed with his two fingers."
"3050","2560/1 - Ahmad ibn Mani said: Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Faid al-Abdi Abu al-Warqa, from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when a boy came to him with a sister of his, and said: O Messenger of Allah, an orphan boy and an orphan sister of his, feed us from what Allah, mighty and majestic, has fed you; may Allah give you from Himself until you are pleased. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: How good is what you said, O boy. O Bilal, go to our family and bring us what food you find with them. So Bilal, may Allah be pleased with him, brought him twenty-one dates. He said: He placed them in his hand, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pointed with his hand toward his mouth, and we thought he was supplicating. Then he, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Seven for you, seven for your mother, and seven for your sister; take lunch with a date and supper with a date. The boy was among the sons of the Emigrants. When he stood up, Muadh, may Allah be pleased with him, followed him, placed his hand on his head and wiped it, and said: May Allah mend your orphanhood, O boy, and make you a successor of your father. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I saw you, what did you do? He said: O Messenger of Allah, out of mercy for him. He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, no man takes in an orphan, treats his guardianship well, then places his hand on his head, except that Allah, blessed and exalted, records for him a good deed for every hair, expiates from him an evil deed for every hair, and raises him a degree for every hair."
"3051","2560/2 - Al-Harith said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Faid ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, and he mentioned it. 2560/3 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad said in the Musnad: I found in my father's book: Yazid narrated to us, and he mentioned part of this hadith. Abdullah said: My father did not narrate it, because he did not approve the hadith of Faid, and in his view he was abandoned."
"3052","2561 - Al-Harith said: Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mutarrif narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I and the guardian of the orphan will be in Paradise like these two, and he pointed with the index and middle fingers. This is mursal."
"3053","2562 - Yazid, that is Ibn Harun, narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Wasil narrated to us, al-Aswad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Adawi narrated to us, from Hassan ibn Kahin, from al-Ashari, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: No orphan sits with people at their bowl but that a devil draws near to their bowl."
"3054","2563 - Abu Yala said: Zahmawayh narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said ibn Dinar, freedman of the family of al-Zubayr, who said: A trustworthy one informed me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no house of a king or a prophet more noble than a house in which there is an orphan."
"3055","2564 - Sulayman ibn Abd al-Jabbar Abu Ayyub narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us, from Abd al-Salam ibn Ajlan al-Hujaymi, Abu Uthman al-Nahdi narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I am the first for whom the gate of Paradise will be opened, except that a woman will come hastening with me, and I will say to her: What is with you, and who are you? She will say: I am a woman who stayed to raise orphans of mine."
"3056","2565 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Umm Dharrah, from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I and the guardian of the orphan will be in Paradise like these two, and he joined the index and middle fingers, and the one who strives for the orphan, the widow and the poor is like the warrior in the path of Allah, and like the fasting one standing in prayer who does not tire."
"3057","2566 - Abu Musa al-Harawi narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Abd al-Malik ibn Razin, from Bilal, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, there is an orphan in my care, may I beat him? He said: Yes, with the same beating with which you beat your own child."
"3058","Chapter 8: Good character. 2567/1 - Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah said: Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Said narrated to us, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You will never encompass people with your wealth, so let cheerfulness of face and good character from you encompass them."
"3059","2567/2 - Abu Yala said: Ahmad ibn Imran al-Akhnasi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Said narrated to us with it."
"3060","2568 - Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Bashshar ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, met Abu Dharr and said: O Abu Dharr, shall I not guide you to two traits that are lighter on the back and heavier in the Scale? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Upon you is good character and long silence; by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, creatures never acted with the like of them."
"3061","2569/1 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Kilabi narrated to us, Shuayb ibn al-Habhab narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The most complete of the believers in faith are the best of them in character, and good character indeed reaches the rank of fasting and prayer."
"3062","2569/2 - Al-Bazzar said: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us with it."
"3063","2569/3 - Wahb ibn Yahya ibn Firgham al-Qaysi narrated to us, from Zakariyya with it. And he said: We do not know it narrated thus except by Zakariyya."
"3064","2569/4 - Abu Ubaydah ibn Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Zarbi Abu Yahya narrated to us, saying: I heard Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The most complete of the believers in faith is the best of them in character."
"3065","2570 - Abdullah ibn Muti narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, al-Kawthar, that is Ibn Hakim, narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Umm Abd, do you know who is the best of the believers in faith? She said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best of them in manners, the gentle and humble; a servant does not reach the reality of faith until he loves for people what he loves for himself, and until his neighbor is safe from his harms."
"3066","2571 - Al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Aradah narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us, from Makhul, from Abu al-Darda, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: He heard a man reviling a man raising his voice, so he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Obscenity is meanness, and bad treatment of dependents is meanness."
"3067","2572/1 - Al-Tayalisi said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Zayd narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Rashid, freedman of Uthman, narrated to me, my master Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to me, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah Almighty has one hundred and seventeen characters; whoever comes to Allah, mighty and majestic, with one character will enter Paradise."
"3068","2572/2 - Al-Bazzar said: Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us with it."
"3069","2572/3 - Abu Yala said: Ishaq, that is Ibn Abi Israil, narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid narrated to us with it."
"3070","Al-Bazzar narrated it from this path, and said: We do not know it except from this path; Abd al-Wahid is not strong, and Abdullah ibn Rashid is unknown."
"3071","2573 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Abu Makin, who said: I heard Abu Mijlaz say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Asma bint Umays, may Allah be pleased with her, was given the choice: which of your husbands do you choose? She said: I choose so-and-so, the one who died leaving her a widow, and he was the best of them in character, and two had been killed leaving her widowed before him."
"3072","2574/1 - Musaddad and Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah both said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from a man of Juhaynah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best thing given to the believing man is good character, and the worst thing given to a man is an evil heart in a handsome form."
"3073","2574/2 - Abu Yala said: Bundar narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, saying: I heard Abu Ishaq with the like of it, and added: And consider what you dislike people seeing in your house when you do it, then do not do it."
"3074","2575 - Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar from Abu Ishaq, from a man of Muzaynah: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the best thing given to the Muslim man? He said: Good character. He said: Then what is the worst thing given to the Muslim? He said: If you dislike a thing being seen upon you in the gathering of the people, then do not do it in private."
"3075","2576/1 - Abu Bakr said: Sharik narrated to us, from Khalaf ibn Hawshab, from Maymun, who said: I asked Umm al-Darda, may Allah be pleased with her: Did you hear anything from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? She said: Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The first thing placed in the Scale is good character."
"3076","2576/2 - Abd said: Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me with this."
"3077","2576/3 - Ahmad ibn Mani said: Abu Badr narrated to us, from Khalaf ibn Hawshab, from a man of the people of Syria who said: We said to Umm al-Darda, may Allah be pleased with her: Narrate to us something you heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and do not narrate to us anything you heard from other than him. She, may Allah be pleased with her, said: I heard him say, and he mentioned it. Thus they differed over Khalaf ibn Hawshab; the preserved version is what Ata al-Kaykharani narrated, from Umm al-Darda, may Allah be pleased with her, from Abu al-Darda; thus the authors of the Sunan, Ibn Hibban and others brought it."
"3078","2577/1 - Al-Harith said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Ismail, that is Ibn Ayyash, narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydillah, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A man indeed reaches the rank of the fasting, night-praying one through good character, and he is indeed recorded as a tyrant though he owns nothing but his household."
"3079","2577/2 - Ahmad ibn Mani said: al-Haytham ibn Kharijah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us with it."
"3080","2578 - Ahmad ibn Mani and al-Harith both said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr informed us, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Husayn, from Makhul, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, Yazid said: I know it only from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Muadh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man who loves to be praised, and it is as if he feared for himself. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: What prevents you from living praised and dying missed; I was only sent to complete the perfections of morals. Al-Bazzar narrated it from the path of Yazid."
"3081","2579 - Ahmad ibn Mani said: Abu Badr narrated to us, Said ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Muhajir, from Sulayman ibn Habib, from his father, from one of the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about the leader of the God-fearing, and he said: He is the God-fearing one of good character."
"3082","2580 - Al-Harith said: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, Sukayn ibn Abi Siraj narrated to us, saying: I heard Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Bad character corrupts deeds as vinegar corrupts honey."
"3083","2581 - Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Talhah narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: The best of you are the best of you in character."
"3084","2582 - Al-Halbas al-Hanzali al-Tamimi al-Basri narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar narrated to us, from Salam or Ibn Salam al-Khurasani, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever is evil in character torments himself, multiplies his worry and sickens his body; whoever quarrels with men, his dignity departs and his manliness falls."
"3085","2583 - Abd al-Aziz ibn Aban narrated to us, Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Salih Abu al-Khalil, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: Which faith is best? He said: Good character. He repeated to him, and he said: Good character. He repeated a third or fourth time, and he made him either stand or sit. He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: That you meet your brother with a cheerful face. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, kept praising good character, saying: It is from Allah, and disparaging bad character, saying: It is from Satan. Then he said: Do you not look at the redness of his eyes and the swelling of his jugular veins."
"3086","Book of Manners. Chapter 1: Comprehensive matters of manners. 2584 - Al-Harith said: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, Maysarah ibn Abd Rabbih narrated to us, from Abu Aishah al-Sadi, from Yazid ibn Umar, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah and Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressed us, and he mentioned a long hadith, in it: Whoever peeps into his neighbor's house and sees a man's private parts, or a woman's hair, or anything of her body, it is due upon Allah Almighty to admit him into the Fire with the hypocrites who used to seek out women's private matters; he will not leave this world until Allah Almighty exposes him and reveals his private parts to onlookers on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever harms his neighbor without right, Allah forbids him Paradise and his abode is the Fire. Indeed Allah Almighty will ask a man about his neighbor as He asks him about the right of his household; whoever neglects his neighbor's right is not of us. Whoever sleeps with deceit toward his Muslim brother in his heart sleeps and wakes in Allah Almighty's wrath until he repents and returns; if he dies upon that he dies upon other than Islam. Then he, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed whoever deceives us is not of us, until he said that three times. Whoever backbites a Muslim, his fast is nullified and his ablution broken; if he dies while thus, he dies like one who deems lawful what Allah Almighty forbade. Whoever walks with talebearing between two, Allah Almighty will unleash upon him in his grave a fire that burns him till the Day of Resurrection, then admit him into the Fire. Whoever pardons his Muslim brother and swallows his anger, Allah Almighty will give him the reward of a martyr. Whoever wrongs his brother, behaves arrogantly toward him and despises him, Allah Almighty will gather him on the Day of Resurrection in the form of tiny ants whom servants trample with their feet, then he will enter the Fire, and he remains in Allah's wrath until he dies. Whoever defends his Muslim brother against backbiting he hears mentioned about him in a gathering, Allah Almighty will repel from him a thousand gates of evil in this world and the Hereafter; if he does not defend him and is pleased with what they said, upon him is evil like their burden. Whoever says to his slave, or another's slave, or to any Muslim: No answer to your call and no happiness to you, will plunge into the Fire. Whoever harms a Muslim is not of us and we are not of him in this world and the Hereafter. Whoever hears of an indecency and spreads it is like one who committed it; whoever hears of good and spreads it is like one who did it. Whoever honors his Muslim brother only honors his Lord, so what do you think. Whoever is two-faced and two-tongued in this world, Allah will make for him two faces and two tongues in the Fire. Whoever walks in severance between two bears of burden as much as is given in reward to one who reconciles between two, and the curse becomes due upon him until he enters Hell where punishment is doubled for him. Whoever walks to aid his Muslim brother and benefit him has the reward of warriors in Allah Almighty's path. Whoever walks in his backbiting and broadcasts his faults, the first step he takes is as if he places it in Hell, and his private faults will be exposed on the Day of Resurrection before all creatures. Whoever walks to a kinsman or relative for visiting the sick or illness afflicting him, Allah Almighty will give him the reward of a hundred martyrs; if he maintains ties with that, for every step he has forty thousand good deeds, forty million evil deeds are removed from him, and he is raised forty million degrees, as if he worshipped Allah Almighty a hundred thousand years. Whoever walks in corruption among kin and severance between them, Allah is angry with him and curses him, and upon him is like the burden of one who severs kinship. Whoever works at separation between a woman and her husband bears Allah's curse in this world and the Hereafter, and Allah forbids him looking at His Face. Whoever leads a blind man to the mosque or to his home or to one of his needs, for every foot he lifts or puts down is recorded the freeing of a slave, and the angels pray for him until he leaves him. Whoever walks with a blind man for a need until he fulfills it, Allah will grant him acquittal from the Fire and acquittal from hypocrisy, decree for him seventy thousand needs of this world, and he keeps wading in mercy until he returns. Whoever walks for a weak person for a need or benefit, Allah Almighty will give him his book in his right hand. Whoever neglects his family and severs his kin, Allah Almighty will deprive him of good recompense on the Day Allah recompenses the doers of good, and he will be gathered with the ruined until he brings a way out, and how can there be a way out. Whoever relieves his brother of a distress of this world, Allah will relieve him of distresses of this world and the Hereafter, and look at him with a look of mercy by which he attains Paradise. Whoever walks in reconciling a woman and her husband has the reward of a thousand martyrs truly killed in Allah's path, and for every step the worship of seventy years: its fasting and its night prayer. Whoever does good to his brother then reminds him of it nullifies his reward and disappoints his effort. Indeed Allah Almighty has forbidden Paradise to the reminder of favors, the miser, the arrogant, the slanderer, the coarse loudmouth, the insolent, the cruel, the base-born, and the alcoholic. Whoever builds a building on a roadside sheltering the traveler, Allah will raise him on the Day of Resurrection with a pearl on his forehead and his face shining for the assembled, until they say: This is an angel among angels; none like him was seen, until he vies with Ibrahim, peace be upon him, in Paradise; forty thousand men will enter Paradise by his intercession. Whoever digs a well until its water flows and offers it to Muslims has the reward of everyone who performs ablution from it and prays, and for the number of hairs of everyone who drinks from it are good deeds, human or jinn, beast or predator or bird or other than that; for every hair therein is the freeing of a slave; there will come to his intercession on the Day of Resurrection at the Basin, the Basin of Holiness, the number of the stars of the sky. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the Basin of Holiness? He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: My Basin, my Basin, my Basin. Whoever intercedes for his brother for a need of his, Allah looks at him, and it is due upon Allah Almighty not to punish a servant He looked at, if that was by his request that he intercede for him; if he intercedes for him without request, he has with that the reward of seventy martyrs. Whoever visits his Muslim brother, for every step until he returns has the freeing of a hundred thousand slaves, the erasure of a hundred thousand evil deeds, and a hundred thousand degrees recorded for him. So we said to Abu Hurayrah: Did not the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever frees a slave, it is his ransom from the Fire? He said: Yes, and the rest of them will be raised for him in the treasures of the Throne with his Lord, blessed and exalted. This long hadith is fabricated against the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; the accused in it is Maysarah ibn Abd Rabbih, no blessing in him."
"3087","Chapter 2: Prohibition of women entering baths. 2585 - Ibn Shirwayh said: Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abu Mamar narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, a man called Ata ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day must not enter the bath with his wife. Al-Bukhari said: Ata ibn Ajlan of Basra, Abd al-Warith named him as his lineage, is rejected in hadith. I say: I brought it for the strangeness of its wording; otherwise Ahmad brought it from the hadith of Ibn Lahiah from Abu al-Zubayr with the wording: let him not enter the bath with his wife; the meaning of the text we cited gives other than the meaning of this."
"3088","Chapter 3: Encouragement of pardon. 2586 - Ahmad ibn Mani said: Abu Nasr al-Tammar narrated to us, Kawthar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: It has reached us that when it is the Day of Resurrection, a caller will call: Where are the people of pardon? He said: Allah Almighty will recompense them for their pardoning of people."
"3089","Chapter 4: Apology. 2587 - Al-Harith said: Hafs ibn Hamzah narrated to us, Sayf ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Umarah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If one's Muslim brother apologizes to him and he does not accept his excuse, he will come on the Day of Resurrection bearing like what the collector of taxes bears, meaning the tithe-taker."
"3090","2588 - Abu Yala said: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from a shaykh called Tariq, from Amr ibn Malik al-Ruasi, who said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, be pleased with me. He turned away three times. I said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, the Lord, blessed and exalted, is entreated for pleasure and He is pleased, so be pleased with me. He said: So he was pleased with me."
"3091","Chapter 5: Prohibition of pursuing private faults. 2589 - Abu Yala said: Ibrahim ibn Dinar narrated to us, Musab ibn Sallam narrated to us, from Hamzah al-Zayyat, from Abu Ishaq al-Sabii, from al-Bara ibn Azib, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressed us until he made the cloistered virgins hear in their houses, or in their chambers, saying: O company of those who believed with their tongues, do not backbite the Muslims nor pursue their private faults; whoever pursues his brother's private fault, Allah will pursue his private fault; whoever Allah, mighty and majestic, pursues his private fault will expose him inside his house."
"3092","Chapter 6: Etiquette of sleep. 2590 - Ibn Abi Umar said: al-Muqri narrated to us, from al-Ifriqi, Umarah ibn Ghurab narrated to me, saying: An aunt of his narrated to him that she asked Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, and mentioned the hadith. She said: I shall inform you what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did: It was my night with him, so I ground some barley and made a round loaf for him. He returned and closed the door; when he, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wanted to sleep he would lock the door, tie the waterskin, turn over the cup and dish, and extinguish the lamp. I waited for him to finish from his prayer place so I could feed him the loaf, but he did not return until sleep overcame me. A tame sheep of our neighbor came, took it, then dragged it away. He said: I became uneasy, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, woke up, so I hastened with it to the door. He said: Take what you can of your loaf, and do not harm your neighbor regarding his sheep."
"3093","2591 - Musaddad said: Hammad narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, from one of the family of Umm Salamah, who said: The bedding of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was like what a man is placed upon in his grave, and the mosque was at his head. Mursal hasan."
"3094","Chapter 7: Dislike of sleep after Asr. 2592 - Abu Yala said: Amr ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, Ibn Ulathah narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever sleeps after Asr and his mind is snatched, let him blame none but himself."
"3095","Chapter 8: Looking in the mirror, etiquette of kohl, sandals and beginning with the right. 2593 - Abu Yala said: Amr ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Ala narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, who said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, looked in the mirror he said: Praise be to Allah who made my form and character good, and adorned of me what He disfigured of others. When he applied kohl he put two in each eye and one between them; when he wore his sandals he began with the right, and when he removed he removed the left; when he entered the mosque he entered his right foot, and he loved beginning with the right in everything, in taking and giving. Yahya ibn al-Ala is very weak."
"3096","Chapter 9: What to say when asked how you woke. 2594 - Abu Yala said: Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Habib, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, who said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: How did you wake? He said: Well, better than people who did not visit a sick person nor attend a funeral."
"3097","Chapter 10: Sneezing and manners in it. 2595 - Abu Yala said: Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Muawiyah, that is Ibn Yahya, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever narrates a narration and sneezes at it, it is true."
"3098","2596 - Muhammad ibn Abi Mashar narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: A man sneezed with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: What shall I say, O Messenger of Allah? He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Say: Praise be to Allah. The people said: What shall we say to him, O Messenger of Allah? He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Say: May Allah have mercy on you. The man said: What shall I reply to them? He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: May Allah guide you and set right your state."
"3099","Chapter 11: Poetry. 2597 - Abu Bakr said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would quote from poems. Al-Bazzar brought it from the path of Abu Usamah and said: Zaidah is alone in it; the narration of others from Simak is from Ikrimah from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her."
"3100","2598 - Abu Yala said: Ibn Abi Shaybah and Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, saying: Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yaqub ibn Utbah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, affirmed as true Umayyah ibn Abi al-Salt in a verse of his poetry. He said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: He spoke the truth. He said: and unless she is flogged, the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: He spoke the truth."
"3101","2599 - Al-Harith said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, who said: Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, said: May Allah have mercy on Labid, he said: their sides. My father used to say: May Allah have mercy on Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her; how would it be if she saw our time."
"3102","2600 - Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Hudhayl ibn Masud al-Bahili narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Said ibn Dukhan, from a man of Hudhayl, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: This poetry is a weighty part of Arab speech; the beggar is given by it, anger is suppressed by it, and by it people reach their aim in their assembly."
"3103","2601 - Abu Yala said: Ibrahim ibn Said narrated to us, Shabab narrated to us, from Abu Bakr al-Hudhali, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, permitted pre-Islamic poetry except the ode of Umayyah ibn Abi al-Salt about the people of Badr, and the ode of al-Asha about Amir and Alqamah."
"3104","2602 - Al-Jarrah narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Sulayman al-Khurasani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhriz al-Azdi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: That one's belly be filled with pus, or blood, is better for him than that it be filled with poetry by which I was lampooned."
"3105","2603 - Abbad ibn Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about poetry, and he said: It is speech; its good is good and its ugly is ugly."
"3106","2604 - Abu Yala said: Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu al-Jahm al-Wasiti, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Imru al-Qays is the banner-bearer of poets to the Fire."
"3107","2605/1 - Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir and Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Sulayman ibn Amr ibn al-Ahwas, Abu Hilal narrated to me, from Abu Barzah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: We were with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a journey, when he heard two men singing, one saying to his companion, and he mentioned poetry. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Who are these two? It was said to him: So-and-so and so-and-so. He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: May Allah Almighty overturn them in tribulation and thrust them into the Fire."
"3108","2605/2 - Abu Bakr said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, and he mentioned it; in it, that he heard Abu Barzah al-Aslami narrate that they were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and heard singing, so they looked toward it. A man stood and listened, and that was before wine was forbidden. He came to them, then returned and said: This is so-and-so and so-and-so, singing, one answering the other, saying. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, raised his hands and said: May Allah overturn them in tribulation; O Allah, thrust them into the Fire."
"3109","Chapter 12: Giving to the poet. 2606 - Abu Dawud said: Yaqub al-Taifi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Nujayd ibn Imran ibn Husayn, from his father, who said: He gave to a poet, and it was said to him: O Abu Nujayd, do you give to a poet? He said: I ransom my honor from him."
"3110","2607 - Musaddad said: Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Muhammad ibn Ali, who said: A man praised Allah Almighty and praised His Messenger, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave him for his praise of Allah, mighty and majestic, who created him, and did not give him for his praise of himself."
"3111","2608 - Abu Bakr said: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from al-Aswad ibn Sari, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, I praised Allah with a praise and praised you with another. He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Bring it, and begin with the praise of Allah Almighty."
"3112","Chapter 13: Command to conceal sin, even if small. 2609 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Abu Hayyan, my father narrated to me, from Maryam bint Tariq, who said: I entered upon Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, and mentioned the hadith. She said: A woman said: O Mother of the Believers, my tenant touches my leg. She turned her face away from her and said: Take her out, so the woman was taken out from her. Then she turned to the women and said: O believing women, what prevents a woman, when she commits a sin and it is concealed for her, from concealing what Allah, mighty and majestic, concealed, and not disclosing to people; people reproach and do not amend, while Allah amends and does not reproach."
"3113","Chapter 14: Encouragement to guard tongue and private parts. 2610 - Abu Bakr said: Mualla ibn Mansur narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Uqayl, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Abu Musa, who said: I and Abu al-Darda, may Allah be pleased with him, were with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he said: Whoever guards what is between his jaws and his legs will enter Paradise. Al-Bukhari brought it in his Tarikh, from Ali ibn al-Madini, from Mualla ibn Mansur with it, saying: Abd al-Ghaffar, meaning Ibn Dawud al-Harrani, did not tell me from Musa ibn Ayan with this chain; intending that he made it from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, dropping Uqayl. But we narrated it in the Fawaid of Tammam from the path of Abu Salih al-Harrani, that is Abd al-Ghaffar, making it with the affirmation of Uqayl; likewise al-Khatib brought it from the path of Muafa ibn Sulayman, from Musa ibn Ayan."
"3114","Chapter 15: Prohibition of anger. 2611 - Musaddad said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Said, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me a deed by which I enter Paradise, and be brief. He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not get angry. I say: Its men are the men of the Sahih, but it is anomalous; the preserved is from Abu Hurayrah, not from Abu Said, may Allah be pleased with him, as it is in the Sahih."
"3115","2612 - Abu Yala said: Dawud ibn Amr narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Urwah, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me a saying, and be brief, that I may grasp it. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not get angry. I repeated twice, each time the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, replied to me: Do not get angry. This chain is hasan."
"3116","Chapter 16: Exhortation to thank blessings. 2613 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from al-Saib ibn Umar, from Yahya ibn Abdullah ibn Sayfi, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever is granted a blessing of truth must repay it; if he has no repayment with him, let him show praise; if he does not, he has been ungrateful."
"3117","2614/1 - Bishr narrated to us, Umarah narrated to us, a man of my people narrated to me, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever is given a gift and finds means, let him repay it; if he does not find, let him praise it; whoever praises it has thanked it, whoever conceals it has been ungrateful for it. Whoever adorns himself with what he was not given is like the wearer of two garments of falsehood. Bishr moved the index and middle fingers."
"3118","2614/2 - Al-Harith said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Aban narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Said, freedman of the Ansar, from Jabir ibn Abdullah with the like of it."
"3119","2615 - Ahmad ibn Mani said: Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Rishdin narrated to us, from Abu Abdillah, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Two traits, whoever has them Allah Almighty records him thankful and patient: whoever looks to one above him in his religion and follows him, and whoever looks to one below him in his worldly life and praises Allah Almighty for preferring him over him. And two traits, whoever has them Allah does not record him patient nor thankful: whoever looks to one above him in his religion and does not follow him, and looks to one above him in his worldly life and grieves over him."
"3120","Chapter 17: Merit of leading the blind. 2616 - Ahmad ibn Mani said: Yusuf ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever leads a blind man forty or fifty cubits, the freeing of a slave is recorded for him."
"3121","2617 - Abu Yala said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Salm ibn Salim narrated to us, from Ali ibn Urwah, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, raised: Whoever leads a blind man forty steps, Paradise becomes due for him. I say: These two hadiths are very weak, and nothing of this is established."
"3122","Chapter 18: Merit of visiting brothers. 2618 - Abu Yala said: Husayn ibn Yazid al-Tahhan al-Kufi narrated to us, Said ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, from al-Sari ibn Ismail, from al-Shabi, from Kab ibn Ujrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Shall I not inform you of your men among the people of Paradise? The Prophet is in Paradise, the martyr is among the people of Paradise, the truthful is among the people of Paradise, the newborn is among the people of Paradise, and the man who visits his brother for Allah Almighty's sake in a distant part of the town is in Paradise."
"3123","2619 - Abu Bakr said: Said ibn Yahya narrated to us, from al-Dahhak ibn Hamrah, from Hammad ibn Jafar, from Maymun ibn Siyah, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No servant visits a brother of his for Allah Almighty's sake but that Allah Almighty says to him in the dominion of His Throne: My servant visited Me; upon Me is his hospitality, and I will not be pleased with hospitality for My servant except in Paradise."
"3124","2620 - Abu Yala said: Abu Bakr narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Abdullah ibn Dhakwan, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Whoever is in the aid of his brother, Allah, mighty and majestic, will be in his aid as long as he is in his brother's aid; whoever releases a ring, Allah will release from him on the Day of Resurrection."
"3125","2621 - Al-Harith said: Yala narrated to us, Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever does not show mercy to our young nor honor our old is not of us."
"3126","2622 - Abu Asim narrated to us, from Talhah ibn Amr, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Visit at intervals, you will increase in love."
"3127","Chapter 19: Merit of modesty. 2623 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, Qays narrated to me, saying: Uyaynah ibn al-Mundhir, may Allah be pleased with him, was sitting with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with another man with him, and some of his wives with him. That man asked for a drink and was brought a drink; when he took to drink they screened him. Uyaynah said: O Messenger of Allah, what is this? He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: This is a trait Allah Almighty gave a people and withheld from you: this is modesty. This is mursal; its men are the men of the Sahih."
"3128","2624 - Al-Tayalisi said: Talhah narrated to us, from Ata, from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to her: O Aishah, if indecency were a man it would be an evil man. Abu al-Shaykh narrated it, adding: And if modesty were a man it would be a righteous man."
"3129","2625 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Malik, who said: I heard Salamah ibn Safwan narrate, from Yazid ibn Talhah ibn Rukanah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Every religion has a character, and the character of Islam is modesty. This is mursal."
"3130","2626 - Qazah ibn Suwayd narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, who said: I passed by a Bedouin, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The first things lifted from this nation are modesty and faith, so ask them of Allah Almighty."
"3131","2627 - Abu Yala said: Muhammad ibn Abi Saminah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Dawud, that is Ibn Abdillah al-Awdi, narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, who said: I and a companion of mine entered upon a man of the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called Usayr, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Modesty brings nothing but good."
"3132","Chapter 20: Prohibition of lying and wrongdoing. 2628/1 - Abu Yala said: Muhammad ibn Jami narrated to us, Maslamah ibn Alqamah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from al-Zibriqan, from al-Nawwas ibn Saman, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Lying is not proper except in three: lying in war, and war is deception; a man lying between two men to reconcile between them; and a man lying to his wife to please her. Yahya ibn Abi Zaidah differed from him, narrating it from Dawud, from Shahr, mursal. Dawud differed from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, narrating it from Shahr, from Asma bint Yazid; Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated it from Ibn Khuthaym, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid; Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated it from Ibn Khuthaym at length."
"3133","2628/2 - Ishaq said: Abd al-Ala ibn Abd al-Ala Abu Hammam informed us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, who said: He was sent."
"3134","2628/3 - Abu Yala said: Ahmad ibn Ayyub al-Dabbi narrated to us, Maslamah ibn Alqamah narrated to us with this chain, saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent an expedition; they passed a man of the desert people and said: O Bedouin, slaughter a sheep for us. He said: He brought them a young goat of his sheep, and they slaughtered it. He said: They kept cooking and roasting until midday, while he shaded with his shade over his sheep. They said: O Bedouin, bring out your sheep so we may nap in the shade. He said: I adjure you by Allah, for they are pregnant; if I bring them out and the hot wind strikes them they will miscarry. They said: Our lives are dearer to us than your sheep. He said: So they brought them out, the hot wind struck them, and they miscarried. He said: Then they left him and went until they came to Madinah, and he had preceded them to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him of the news. When they came, he, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, asked them about what he mentioned, and they denied. He singled out a man of them and said: O so-and-so, if there is no good in your companions, perhaps there is with you; tell me the truth. He said: The Bedouin spoke the truth, O Messenger of Allah; the news is as he said. He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do you plunge into lying as moths plunge into fire; every lie is written inevitably, except that a man lies in war, for war is deception, or lies between two men to reconcile between them, or a man lies to his wife to please her."
"3135","2629 - Abu Yala said: Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Ayyash, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent an expedition to the outskirts of Mudar; they camped on desert land. In the morning they saw a tent with pastured sheep in its yard. They came to the owner of the sheep, stood over him and said: Slaughter for us. He brought out a sheep for them and they disdained it, then he brought out another sheep and they disdained it. He said: There is nothing in my sheep but its stud or a suckling ewe. They took a sheep of the flock. When midday came, with no shade to shelter from the heat, in a land with no shade, while the Bedouin had kept his sheep in its shade, they said: We are more deserving of the shade than these sheep. They came to him and said: Bring out your sheep sheltered in this shade. He said: If you bring out my sheep they will sicken and cast their young; I am a man who paid zakat and became Muslim. They brought out his sheep, and within an hour they bleated and cast their young. The Bedouin hastened until he came to Madinah to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him of what was done to him. He was intensely angry at that, then seated him until the people came, and he asked them; they said: He lied. Some of the Messenger of Allah's anger was relieved. The Bedouin said: By the One by Whom I swear, I hope Allah will inform you of my news and theirs. It occurred to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he was truthful, so he took them aside man by man; when he took aside a man of them he adjured him by Allah Almighty to narrate to him as the Bedouin narrated to him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood and said: O people, let it not carry you to follow one another in lying as moths follow one another into fire; every lie is recorded against the son of Adam except three traits: a man lying to his wife so she is pleased with him, the hadith. Maslamah ibn Alqamah narrated it from Dawud, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from al-Nawwas also at length."
"3136","2630 - Abu Yala said: Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Ziyad ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, from Nafi ibn al-Harith, Abu Barzah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to us, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Indeed lying blackens the face, and talebearing is the punishment of the grave."
"3137","Chapter 21: Censure of lying, praise of truthfulness. 2631 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydillah ibn Umar, from Umar ibn Atiyyah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Dallaf, from his uncle, from Bilal ibn al-Harith, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: Let neither a man's prayer nor his fasting deceive you; but when he speaks he is truthful, when entrusted he fulfills, and when on the verge of sin he is pious. This is mawquf sahih."
"3138","2632 - Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Nothing of lying is proper, in earnest or in jest. Mawquf sahih."
"3139","2633/1 - Abu Bakr said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us. 2633/2 - Ahmad ibn Mani said: Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, both saying: al-Layth narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Sad, that is Ibn Sinan, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Guarantee for me six, I will guarantee Paradise for you. It was said: What are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: When you speak, do not lie; when you promise, do not break; when entrusted, do not betray; lower your gazes, guard your private parts, and restrain your hands."
"3140","Chapter 22: Leaning on a staff. 2634 - Al-Harith said: Muhammad ibn Umar narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Kathir narrated to us, from Musa ibn Nuaym, freedman of Zayd ibn Thabit, from his father, from Zayd ibn Thabit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to lean on a stalk of Ibn Tab dates; Zayd used to lean on it in his house and on his way to his properties."
"3141","Chapter 23: Etiquette of riding. 2635 - Al-Harith said: Muhammad narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Utbah ibn Tamim, from al-Walid ibn Amir, from Urwah ibn Mutib, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, decreed that the owner of the mount has most right to its front. This is mursal daif, but it has witnesses."
"3142","2636/1 - Musaddad said: Khalid narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Muwarriq, from a freedman of theirs, who said: al-Husayn ibn Ali and Abdullah ibn Jafar, may Allah be pleased with them, met the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, placed one before him and the other behind him."
"3143","2636/2 - Maslamah ibn Alqamah narrated to us, from Dawud, from Muwarriq, from a freedman of Banu Hashim, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came from a journey, and Abdullah ibn Jafar and al-Husayn ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with them, met him; he, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, placed the elder behind him and carried the younger before him. Thus Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated it; Asim differed from him, narrating it from Muwarriq, from Abdullah ibn Jafar, may Allah be pleased with him; Ibn Abi Shaybah and others brought it."
"3144","2637/1 - Abu Yala said: Abu Hisham Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Rifah narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Mujammi, Uthman ibn Kab, that is al-Qurazi, narrated to me, from a man called Rufay, from Safiyyah bint Huyayy, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mounted me behind him on the rear of his she-camel at night; I began to doze, so he would touch me, saying: O you, O daughter of Huyayy, O Safiyyah."
"3145","2637/2 - Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, the like of it."
"3146","2638 - Abu Yala said: al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Fudayl narrated to us, Faid narrated to us, Ubaydillah ibn Ali ibn Abi Rafi narrated to me, from Abu Rafi, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came one day from Khaybar, having mounted Safiyyah bint Huyayy, may Allah be pleased with her, behind him on his saddlebag, with Abu Rafi, may Allah be pleased with him, on a camel. When we drew near Madinah, he said: O Abu Rafi, dismount from the camel and mount Safiyyah upon it, for I fear dawn will break before we enter Madinah. He said: So Abu Rafi walked until he brought her into Madinah."
"3147","2639 - Musaddad said: Mutamir narrated to us, saying: I heard Layth narrate, from Abdullah: Abu al-Darda, may Allah be pleased with him, saw a riding man with a person running behind him, and said: O so-and-so, if only you carried this one behind you. He said: And should I carry this non-Arab behind me. He said: Then send him to where you intend. He said: I will not. He said: Then exchange him for one lighter than him. He said: I will not. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever has a person run behind him while he is riding, Allah Almighty will only increase him in distance."
"3148","2640 - From Layth, from a man: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, saw a man with a person running behind him while he was riding, or that reached him, and said: May Allah split his heart, may Allah split his heart."
"3149","Chapter 24: Reconciliation between people. 2641/1 - Al-Tayalisi said: Abu al-Sabbah al-Shami narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz al-Shami, from his father, from Abu Ayyub, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: O Abu Ayyub, shall I not guide you to a charity that pleases Allah and His Messenger by its giving? He said: Yes. He said: You reconcile between people when they are corrupted, and bring them close when they are distant."
"3150","2641/2 - Ibn Abi Shaybah said: Ubaydillah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Ubadah ibn Umar ibn Ubadah ibn Awf, who said: Abu Ayyub, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Shall I not guide you to a charity Allah, blessed and exalted, and His Messenger, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, love? You reconcile between people when they hate and corrupt one another."
"3151","2641/3 - Abd ibn Humayd said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this."
"3152","2642 - Abd also said: Yala, that is Ibn Ubayd, narrated to us, al-Ifriqi, that is Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn Anum, narrated to us, from a man, from Abdullah ibn Yazid, from Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best charity is mending relations."
"3153","Chapter 25: Naming Allah over everything. 2643 - Abd said: Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Haram ibn Uthman narrated to us, from the two sons of Jabir, from their father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you comes to the door of his chamber, let him mention Allah's name, for his companion of Satan with him will turn back. When you enter your chambers, mention names and their devil dwellers will leave. When you depart, mention names over the first saddlecloth you place on your mounts, so Satan does not share your ride with you; if you do not, he shares with you. When you eat, mention names, so he does not share your food with you; if you do not, he shares your food with you. Do not keep rubbish overnight with you in your chambers, for it is his seat; do not keep the napkin overnight in your houses, for it is his resting place. Do not spread the saddle pads on the backs of mounts, nor dwell in houses without locks, nor sleep on roofs without walls. When you hear a dog's barking and a donkey's braying, seek refuge with Allah, for no donkey brays nor dog barks except when it sees him."
"3154","Chapter 26: Prohibition of wastefulness. 2644 - Abu Yala said: Muadh ibn Shubah of Basra narrated to us, Uthman ibn Matar narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Honor the neighborhood of Allah's blessings; do not drive them away, for seldom do they depart from a people and return to them."
"3155","Chapter 27: Seeking permission. 2645 - Musaddad said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Khalid, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, who said: A man asked Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, about seeking permission upon his parents? He said: Yes, seek permission; would you like to see their nakedness from them."
"3156","2646 - Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, from Abu Ishaq, from Muslim ibn Nudhayr, who said: A man asked Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him: Shall I seek permission upon my mother? He said: If you do not seek permission upon her you will see of her what displeases you."
"3157","2647 - Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade seeking permission facing the door."
"3158","2648 - Al-Harith said: Muhammad ibn Umar narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Sasaah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Sasaah, from al-Harith ibn Abdullah ibn Kab, from Umm Umarah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at al-Jurf on our arrival from Khaybar, saying: Do not come to women at night after the Isha prayer."
"3159","2649 - Abu Yala said: al-Harith ibn Surayj narrated to us, al-Muttalib ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abdillah al-Asbahani narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Malik, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The doors of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, were knocked with fingernails."
"3160","Chapter 28: Greeting. 2650 - Ishaq said, Qabisah ibn Uqbah informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father, who said: Umm Ayman was a slave girl of the mother of Ibrahim, the son of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; when she entered she would say: Peace, not upon you. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, permitted her to say: Peace be upon you."
"3161","Chapter 29: Greeting disbelievers, honoring their elders. 2651 - Musaddad said: Sharik narrated to us, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Kurayb, who said: Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, wrote to a dhimmi, beginning him with peace. I said to him: Do you begin with peace? He said: Allah is Peace."
"3162","2652/1 - Abdullah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Uthman ibn Mawhab, from Abu Burdah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wrote to a man not upon Islam's religion: Peace you are. He wrote to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with peace, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wrote at the end of the letter greeting him."
"3163","2652/2 - Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Amr ibn Uthman, who said: I heard Abu Burdah, may Allah be pleased with him, say: A man of the polytheists wrote to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with peace, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wrote returning peace upon him."
"3164","2653 - Abbad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, who said: Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, wrote to a Persian landlord greeting him in his letter. It was said to him: Do you greet him while he is a disbeliever? He said: He wrote to me greeting me, so I replied to him."
"3165","2654 - Sharik narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, who said: If you have a need of him, begin him with peace. Mujahid said: When you write, write with peace upon whoever follows guidance."
"3166","2655 - Ibn Abi Umar said: Marwan narrated to us, Hassan ibn Abi Yahya al-Kindi narrated to us, from a shaykh of Kindah, who said: We were sitting with Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, when the bishop of Najran came to him, and he made room for him. A man said to him: Do you make room for this Christian, O Commander of the Believers? He, may Allah be pleased with him, said: They, when they came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he made room for them."
"3167","2656 - Abu Yala said: Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Humayd, that is al-Ruasi, narrated to us, from Hasan ibn Salih, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Whoever of Allah's creation greets you, return it upon him even if he is a Magian; Allah Almighty says: When you are greeted with a greeting, greet with better than it, for the people of Islam; or return it, upon the polytheist."
"3168","Chapter 30: Encouragement to conceal secrets. 2657 - Abu Yala said: Jabbarah ibn al-Mughallis narrated to us, Hafs ibn Subayh al-Nasai, among the most worshipful of people, narrated to me, from Malik ibn Dinar, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When a man speaks, then turns, it is a trust. It has a witness from the hadith of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him."
"3169","Chapter 31: Good appearance. 2658 - Ibn Abi Umar said: Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from al-Hadrami ibn Lahiq, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you send a messenger, send him of good face and good name."
"3170","2659 - Abd said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mujabbir informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Seek good with the handsome of face."
"3171","2660 - Abu Yala said: Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Jabrah bint Muhammad ibn Thabit ibn Siba, from her father, from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Seek good with the handsome of faces."
"3172","2661 - Ahmad ibn Mani said: Abbad ibn Abbad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Ziyad, from al-Hajjaj ibn Yazid, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you seek needs, seek them from the handsome of faces."
"3173","Chapter 32: Merit of roughness. 2662 - Abu Bakr said: Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Said narrated to us, from his father, from a man of Aslam called Ibn al-Adra, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Live like Mad, be rough, walk barefoot, and practice archery."
"3174","Chapter 33: Censure of talebearing. 2663 - Ishaq said: Ubaydillah ibn Musa informed us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah al-Rabadhi, from Ayyub ibn Khalid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, who said: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The worst of people are three: a man arrogant toward his parents, belittling them; a man who strives in corruption between a man and a woman, aiding him against her without right until he separates them, then marries her after him; and a man who strives in corruption between people with lies until they become enemies and hate one another."
"3175","2664 - Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid informed us, saying: I found in my book from Habib ibn Najih, from some people of Madinah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, who said: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Three Allah Almighty curses on the Day of Resurrection: a man who turns away from his parents; another who strives to separate a man and a woman to marry her after him; and another who carries tales among believers to make them enemies and hate one another."
"3176","2665 - Abu Yala said: Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Shahr, from Asma bint Yazid, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O people, shall I not inform you of the best of you? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best of you, when seen Allah is remembered and their hearts find rest. Shall I not inform you of the worst of you? They said: Yes. He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The worst of you are those who walk with talebearing, corrupting between loved ones, seeking hardship for the innocent."
"3177","2666/1 - Ibn Abi Umar said: Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever is two-tongued in this world, Allah will make for him two tongues of fire on the Day of Resurrection."
"3178","2666/2 - Abu Yala said: Humayd ibn Masadah narrated to us, from Ararah ibn al-Birind, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from al-Hasan and Qatadah, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, and he mentioned it."
"3179","2666/3 - Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Muslim, and he mentioned it."
"3180","Chapter 34: Backbiting. 2667 - Ahmad ibn Mani said: Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from Muadh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man was mentioned with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and it was said: How helpless he is. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You backbit your brother. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we said what is in him. He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If you said what is not in him, you slandered him."
"3181","2668 - Abu Dawud said: Hammam narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Haddad, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Maiz ibn Malik came, and he mentioned the hadith of his stoning. He said: Two men came upon him and said: Woe to this one; Allah covered him and he did not cover himself, so he was driven as a dog is driven. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came upon a carcass and said: Bite of this carcass. They said: O Messenger of Allah, this carcass we cannot bear. He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What you took of your brother is fouler than this carcass. Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah followed him, from Abu al-Zubayr; Ibn Hibban brought it from his path."
"3182","2669 - Abu Bakr said: Abu Khalid, not al-Ahmar, narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: We were sitting with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when a man stood and a man after him spoke ill of him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Pick your teeth. He said: Of what shall I pick, O Messenger of Allah? I did not eat meat to pick. He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Yes, of your brother's flesh you ate just now."
"3183","2670/1 - Ahmad ibn Mani said: Qurran ibn Tammam narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd, from Musa ibn Wardan, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him: We were sitting with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when a man of the people said: O Messenger of Allah, how helpless is so-and-so. He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You ate your brother's flesh and backbit him."
"3184","2670/2 - Abu Yala said: Amr al-Naqid narrated to us, Qurran narrated to us with it."
"3185","2671 - Musaddad said: Ismail narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, who said: Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, used to say: Backbiting is that you mention of your brother the worst you know in him; if you mention what is not in him, that is slander. The hadith of al-Bara, may Allah be pleased with him, preceded in the prohibition of pursuing private faults."
"3186","Chapter 35: What is permitted of backbiting and its expiations. The hadith of Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him: What an evil servant of Allah is so-and-so, in the merits of Khalid ibn al-Walid, may Allah be pleased with him. 2672 - Al-Harith said: A man narrated to us, Anbasah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The expiation of backbiting is that you seek forgiveness for whom you backbit."
"3187","Chapter 36: Censure of pride, praise of humility. 2673/1 - Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah said: Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Shall I not teach you what Nuh taught his son? They said: Yes. He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O my son, I command you with two matters and forbid you two matters: I forbid you to associate anything with Allah, for whoever associates anything with Allah, Allah has forbidden him Paradise; and I forbid you pride, for none enters Paradise with a mustard grain of pride in his heart. I command you to say: There is no god but Allah, alone without partner; His is dominion and His is praise, and He is over all things Capable; if the heavens were a ring it would split it. I command you with glory be to Allah and His praise, for it is the prayer of creation and the glorification of creation, and by it creation is provided. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, is it of pride that a man has a mount he rides, or a garment he wears, or food he invites his companions to? He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No, but pride is to belittle truth and despise people. I shall inform you of five: whoever has them is not arrogant: hobbling the sheep, wearing wool, riding the donkey, sitting with the poor believers, and a man's eating with his family."
"3188","2673/2 - Abd said: Ubaydillah ibn Musa narrated to us, Musa ibn Ubaydah narrated to us with it. Musa is weak; al-Saqab ibn Zuhayr differed from him, narrating it from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them."
"3189","2674/1 - Abu Yala said: Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Mawsili narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from al-Saqab ibn Zuhayr, from Zayd ibn Aslam, referring it to Abdullah ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, who said: A Bedouin man came wearing a cloak of Sijan buttoned with gold, and he mentioned the hadith; in it: Nuh said to his son, and he mentioned it. The rest comes, Allah Almighty willing, in the merits of the Chosen, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; it has another path from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them."
"3190","2674/2 - Al-Bazzar said: Ibrahim ibn Said narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, raised: Shall I not inform you of Nuh's bequest, peace be upon him, and he mentioned it."
"3191","Al-Harith said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Talhah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say on the Day of Resurrection: I made a lineage, and you made a lineage; I made the most noble of you the most God-fearing of you, while you say: O son of so-and-so, I am nobler than you. Today I raise My lineage and lower your lineage. Where are the God-fearing?"
"3192","Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Al-Haytham ibn Kharijah narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubayd Allah, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man may attain the rank of the fasting, night-praying person through forbearance, yet he is recorded as a tyrant while he owns nothing but his household."
"3193","Abd said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Salim ibn Ubayd informed us, from Abu Abd Allah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, who said that he heard Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no man on earth who dies with even a mustard seed's weight of pride in his heart except that Allah will place him in the Fire. An Ansari man said: O Messenger of Allah, I love beauty, in my sword harness, in washing my clothes of dirt, and in the beauty of my sandal straps and sandals. He said: That is not what I mean; pride is only rejecting the truth and despising people. He said: O Prophet of Allah, what is rejecting the truth and despising people? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rejecting the truth is that you have wealth owed upon a man, and he denies it and claims nothing is due upon him, so a man commands him to fear Allah and he refuses; as for despising, it is one who comes to people with his nose held high in arrogance, and when he sees the weak and poor he does not greet them nor sit with them out of contempt for them; that is the one who despises people. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever patches his garment, repairs his sandal, rides the donkey, visits the slave when he is sick, and milks the sheep has freed himself of arrogance. The rest of this hadith will come, Allah willing, in the Virtues, in the biography of Abdullah ibn Qays al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him."
"3194","Ahmad said in al-Zuhd: Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Mutarrif, from Ka'b, who said: There is no human except that in his head is a bridle in the hand of an angel; if he humbles himself, it raises him, and if he is arrogant, it lowers him."
"3195","Al-Harith said: Yazid narrated to us, Asim ibn Muhammad al-Umari narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, I know it only as raised to the Prophet: He says: Whoever humbles himself to Me like this, I raise him like this. And he turned the inside of his palm toward the earth, then turned the inside of his palm toward the heaven and raised it toward the heaven."
"3196","Abd al-Aziz ibn Aban narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man sought permission in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Give permission to the retainer of al-Nu'man ibn al-Mundhir. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your great ones are more insignificant to Allah than the dung beetles that push filth with their noses. He said: Then a man sought permission and said: My praise is an adornment and my blame is a disgrace. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have lied; that belongs to Allah, Blessed and Exalted."
"3197","Abu Ya'la said: Al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abbad ibn Abbad ibn Alqamah narrated to us, from Abu Mijlaz, that the companions of Ibn Mas'ud were pinched by cold, and they were shy to come out in cloaks and outer garments, so he missed them, and it was said to him: Their situation is such-and-such. So Abu Abd al-Rahman appeared in the morning wearing a cloak, and they said: Ibn Mas'ud has appeared in a cloak. Then the second day came, then the third day came, and when they saw him in the cloak, they came in their garments together, and he recognized faces he had missed. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No one with a mustard seed's weight of pride in his heart will enter Paradise, or he said: a speck of pride."
"3198","Chapter: The virtue of removing harm from the road. Abu Ya'la said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, Al-Minhal ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated a hadith to us, and we never rejoiced at anything after Islam more than our joy at it. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is rewarded for removing harm from the road, for guiding to the way, for expressing on behalf of the speech-impaired, and for lending milk; even for goods wrapped in his garment which he feels for and his hand misses."
"3199","Chapter: Spitting is permitted. Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abu Nasr, meaning Ibn Hilal, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I have not spat to my right since I became Muslim. It was said to Sufyan: Not in prayer nor otherwise? He said: Yes."
"3200","Al-Harith said: Muhammad ibn Umar narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Umar al-Hatibi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'd ibn Zurarah narrated to us, from Sawdah bint Harithah, wife of Amr ibn Hazm, from Amr ibn Hazm, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spit to his right, to his left, and in front of him."
"3201","Chapter: Cutting bells off animals. Musaddad said: Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Husayn al-Mu'allim, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, who said: Hawt ibn Abd al-Uzza narrated to me, who said: A caravan came from Mudar with a bell in it, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that they cut it off; from then the bell was disliked. And he said: The angels do not accompany a caravan in which there is a bell."
"3202","Chapter: With whom one begins in a letter. Musaddad said: Hammad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, who said: Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, wrote to Amir ibn Abd Allah: From Abdullah ibn Qays to Amir ibn Abd Allah, who is called Ibn Abd Qays: To proceed: If you have changed, then return; if you have not changed, then continue. Peace be upon you."
"3203","Chapter: What belongs to women on the road. Abu Ya'la said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Umar ibn Ali narrated to us, from Abdullah, meaning Ibn Sa'id al-Maqburi, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The side of the road does not belong to women, meaning its middle."
"3204","Chapter: Guarding the concealment of secrets. Abu Ya'la said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Habib ibn Hajar narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I left the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heading toward my family, and I passed by boys playing, and their play pleased me, so I stood watching the boys. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me and stood over them and greeted the boys, then he sent me on an errand of his. I returned to my mother after the time I used to return to them, and my mother said: What kept you today, my son? I said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me on an errand. She said: What errand? I said: Mother, it is a secret. She said: My son, then guard the secret of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Thabit said: I said to Anas: O Abu Hamzah, do you still remember that errand today? He said: I remember it well; had I told it to anyone I would have told it to you, O Thabit."
"3205","Ibn Abi Umar said: Sufyan narrated to us, a shaykh from the people of Kufa narrated to us, who said: I went with Thabit to Anas, and I heard him say to him: I have a secret from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); had I told it to anyone among people I would have told it to you. And in the chapter of greeting is the hadith of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, concerning it."
"3206","Abu Ya'la said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Abi Yazid narrated to us, Abbad al-Minqari narrated to us, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me, and it was the first thing he advised me with: O my son, conceal my secret and you will be a believer. My mother and the wives of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to ask me about the secret of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but I would not tell them, and I will never tell the secret of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to anyone ever. The hadith."
"3207","Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Yazid, that is Ibn Harun, narrated to us, Al-Ala' Abu Muhammad informed us, Anas narrated it similarly."
"3208","Chapter: Two should not converse privately excluding the third. Abu Ya'la said: Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Ward, from al-Hasan ibn Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two should not converse privately excluding the third, for that harms the believer, and Allah dislikes harming the believer."
"3209","Chapter: Greeting. Ishaq said: I said to Abu Usamah: Did Musa ibn Ubaydah al-Rabadhi narrate to you, from Yaqub ibn Zayd, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: Peace be upon you, ten good deeds are written for him; whoever says: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, twenty good deeds are written for him; and whoever says: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, thirty good deeds are written for him? He acknowledged it and said: Yes."
"3210","Abu Bakr said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Musa, with it."
"3211","Ishaq said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah al-Rabadhi, from Ayyub ibn Khalid, from Malik, a man of the Ansar, who said: A group of us gathered and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are people of the highlands and lowlands, and we have sittings in which we talk. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give sittings their due. We said: And what is their due, O Messenger of Allah? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Lower your gazes, return the greeting, guide the blind, enjoin good, and forbid evil. This chain is weak because of Musa."
"3212","Musaddad said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abu Harun, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Peace be upon you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ten. Then another came and said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Twenty. Then another came and said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Thirty. Abu Harun is weak, and it has a witness from the hadith of Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, with Abu Dawud, al-Darimi, and al-Tirmidhi."
"3213","Abu Ya'la said: Abu Hisham al-Rifa'i narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, and Masruq ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, both from Abdullah ibn Sa'id, from his grandfather, that is Abu Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah, Exalted, is al-Salam, so do not begin with anything before Him; when it is said: Peace be upon you, then say: Peace be upon you. And in the narration of Abd al-Salam: When one of you intends the greeting, let him say: Peace; for Allah, Exalted, is al-Salam, so do not begin with anything before Allah."
"3214","Al-Fadl ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Anbasah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Muhammad ibn Zadham, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Greeting comes before speech, and do not invite anyone to food until he greets."
"3215","Al-Harith said: Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, raising it to the Prophet: The rider greets the walker, the walker greets the seated, and when two walkers are together, whichever of them begins with greeting is the better."
"3216","Al-Humaydi and Musaddad both said: Sufyan narrated to us, who said: I heard Zayd ibn Aslam say: My father sent me to Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, and I entered upon him without permission. He said: So he taught me, saying: When you wish to enter, seek permission; if permission is given to you, then greet and enter. What is your need? He said: My father sent me asking you to write for him your valuation in Khaybar for him in exchange for dried cheese. So he wrote for him, and said: Did you stop? I said: Yes."
"3217","Musaddad said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Qanan ibn Abd Allah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsajah, from al-Bara ibn Azib, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Spread greeting among you."
"3218","Abu Bakr said: Malik ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Musa ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Qanan ibn Abd Allah al-Nahmi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsajah, with it. And he added: And coquetry is coquetry."
"3219","Ishaq and Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Qanan narrated to us with it, and he added: Meaning abundance of insolence."
"3220","Ahmad ibn Mani' said: And Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Qanan narrated to us."
"3221","Abu Ya'la said: Ishaq ibn Isra'il narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, with it."
"3222","Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Yazid narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ya'ish ibn al-Walid, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, you will not believe until you love one another. Shall I not inform you of a matter which, if you do it, you will love one another? Spread greeting among you."
"3223","Abu Ya'la said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abi Yazid narrated to us, Abbad al-Minqari narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me, and it was the first thing he advised me with: O my son, conceal my secret and you will be a believer. My mother and the wives of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to ask me about the secret of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but I would not tell them, nor will I ever tell the secret of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to anyone ever. O my son, when you leave your house, let your eye not fall upon anyone of the people of the qiblah except that you greet him, for you will return forgiven. O my son, when you enter your dwelling, greet yourself and your family. O my son, if you can wake and sleep with no cheating in your heart toward anyone, for it is easier for you in the reckoning. O my son, if you follow my advice, let nothing be dearer to you than death."
"3224","Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Yazid, that is Ibn Harun, narrated to us, Al-Ala' Abu Muhammad narrated to us, Anas narrated with it. Al-Tirmidhi brought out part of it through Abdullah ibn Anas, from Ali ibn Zayd, and he mentioned that Abbad al-Minqari narrated it at length from Ali ibn Zayd from Anas, without mentioning Sa'id."
"3225","Chapter: Honoring the stranger, and shyness before the elder. Ibn Abi Shaybah said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Abd al-Muttalib ibn Rabi'ah ibn al-Harith ibn Abd al-Muttalib, who said: My father sent me, and al-Abbas sent his son al-Fadl, to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). We entered upon him, and he seated us to his right and to his left, and he pressed us as severely as you ever see pressing."
"3226","Chapter: Leaving greeting upon one who is praying. Abu Ya'la said: Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Had I entered upon people praying, I would not have greeted them."
"3227","Chapter: Embracing, hugging, and handshaking. Abu Ya'la said: Ishaq narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Khalid ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Bashir narrated to me, So-and-so al-Anazi narrated to me, from Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for me during his illness in which he died. I came to him and found him sleeping, so I leaned over him, and he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his hands and embraced me."
"3228","Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Mujalid narrated to us, from his father, from Amir, that is al-Sha'bi, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When Ja'far, may Allah be pleased with him, came from Abyssinia, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) embraced him."
"3229","Shabab, that is Khalifah ibn Khayyat, narrated to us, Durust ibn Hamzah narrated to us, Matar al-Warraq narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: There are no two servants loving each other for Allah, Exalted, one of whom meets his companion and shakes his hand, and they send blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except that they do not part until their sins are forgiven, past and future."
"3230","Chapter: Kissing the hand. Ibn Abi Umar said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Jud'an, who said: Thabit said to Anas: O Abu Hamzah, did you touch the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with your hand? He said: Yes. He said: Then give it to me. He gave him his hand and he kissed it. Sufyan said: I thought Ibn Jud'an says: I heard Thabit say to Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, and he mentioned it."
"3231","Chapter: Perfume. Al-Harith said: Rawh narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, Hanan al-Asadi narrated to us, from Abu Uthman, who said: When sweet basil is gifted to one of you, let him not refuse it, for it has come out of Paradise. This hadith is mursal, hasan."
"3232","Musaddad said: Isa and Yahya narrated to us, separating them, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far, from the uncle of his father Umar ibn al-Hakam, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not refuse perfume, for it is light to carry and sweet in scent."
"3233","Chapter: One who calls his companion and he answers with Labbayk. Abu Ya'la said: Jabbarah narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Suwayd narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ya'mar, from Ibn Umar, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: A man called the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) three times, each time he answered him: At your service, at your service."
"3234","Chapter: Prohibition of foul speech. Abu Bakr said: Yunus narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ibn Sinan, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two who insult each other, whatever they say is upon the one who began, until the wronged one transgresses."
"3235","Abu Ya'la said: Abu Ali narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, with this."
"3236","Ishaq said: Sufyan informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl, and Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you say: My soul has become wicked; rather let him say: My soul has become heavy. I say: This hadith is sahih; al-Nasa'i narrated it in al-Yawm wa al-Laylah from Qutaybah, from Sufyan. Al-Shaykhan and others brought it from the hadith of Yunus ibn Yazid, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him. Both hadiths are sahih. Abu Umamah saw the Prophet and narrated, his father was a Companion, and something of this chapter has preceded in the virtue of modesty."
"3237","Abu Ya'la said: Sufyan narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not curse the night and the day, nor the sun and the moon, nor the winds, for they are sent as mercy to a people and punishment to a people."
"3238","Abu Musa narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, who said: I heard Yahya ibn Ayyub narrating, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Marthad, from Hassan ibn Kurayb, from Ali, that he used to say: The speaker of foul speech and the one who listens to it are equal in sin."
"3239","Abu Musa narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, who said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrating, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ubayd Allah, who said: I saw Usamah, may Allah be pleased with him, praying at the grave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Marwan ibn al-Hakam came out and said: Do you pray at his grave? He said: I love him. He said an ugly word to him, then turned away. Usamah, may Allah be pleased with him, left and said to Marwan: You have harmed me, and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah, Exalted, hates the foul and the deliberately foul; and you are foul and deliberately foul."
"3240","Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cursing the believer is like killing him, and when one says to him: O disbeliever, it is like killing him."
"3241","Al-Harith said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Awn ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah ibn Mas'ud, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A rooster crowed near the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a man said: O Allah, curse it. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile it nor curse it, for it calls to prayer."
"3242","Abd said: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us, from Salih, from Ubayd Allah, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, similarly. And the correct wording is: from Ubayd Allah, from Zayd ibn Khalid."
"3243","Abu Ya'la said: Abu Yasir al-Mustamli narrated to us, Suwayd Abu Hatim narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a flea bit a man, and he cursed it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not curse it, for it woke a prophet among the prophets for prayer."
"3244","Al-Tabarani said in al-Awsat: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Bashir, from Qatadah, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Fleas were mentioned before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: They awaken for prayer."
"3245","Hashim ibn Marthad narrated to us, Adam narrated to us, Abu Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Tarif, from al-Asbagh ibn Nubatah, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: We stopped at a lodging, and fleas harmed us, so we reviled them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile them, for what an excellent animal; it woke you for the remembrance of Allah, Exalted. It is not narrated from Ali except through this; Adam is alone in it."
"3246","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Sharik ibn Abi Namir, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man traveled with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he cursed his camel. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O servant of Allah, do not travel with us upon a cursed camel."
"3247","Al-Tabarani said in al-Awsat: Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, with it, and he said: Isma'il is alone in it."
"3248","Chapter: Caution and guarding. Ahmad said in al-Zuhd: Surayj and Affan narrated to us, both saying: Mahdi narrated to us, from Ghaylan, from Mutarrif, that he used to say: Guard yourselves against people with bad opinion. I say: This was narrated raised to the Prophet."
"3249","Al-Tabarani said in al-Awsat: Ahmad, meaning Ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir, narrated to us, Dawud ibn Rashid narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Yahya, from Sulayman ibn Muslim, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Guard yourselves against people with bad opinion. And he said: It is not narrated from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, except with this chain; Baqiyyah is alone in it."
"3250","Abu Ya'la said: Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn al-Antaki narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, from Atiyyah ibn Qays, from Abu al-Darda, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Test and you will know little."
"3251","Chapter: Dislike of rhymed prose. Ishaq said: Al-Mula'i informed us, Umar ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Iyas ibn Salamah ibn al-Akwa', from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and some of the people spoke words resembling rhymed verse. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Stand, O Salamah. This chain is hasan."
"3252","Chapter: Prohibition of reviling the dead when it harms the living. Al-Harith said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from one of his companions, who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was traveling, he overlooked the grave of a man whom he named. Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: May Allah curse the owner of this grave, for he was an enemy of Allah. He said: And his son was traveling with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Rather may Allah curse Abu Quhafah, for by Allah, he neither honored the guest nor fought the enemy. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile the dead, lest you harm the living."
"3253","Chapter: Deterrence from overstepping in a Muslim's honor. Ibn Abi Shaybah said: Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Umar ibn Rashid, from Yahya, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah, from al-Bara ibn Azib, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Usury has seventy-two doors, the least of which is like a man approaching his mother, and the worst usury is a man's overstepping in his companion's honor."
"3254","Al-Harith said: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sa'id, from Aban, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has his Muslim brother backbitten in his presence and aids him, Allah will aid him in this world and the Hereafter; and whoever abandons aiding him while able to, Allah will forsake him in this world and the Hereafter."
"3255","Abu Ya'la said: Abd al-Ghaffar narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Abu Isma'il al-Abdi, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said similarly. I say: Abu Isma'il is Aban mentioned before."
"3256","Chapter: Prohibition of tale-bearing against a Muslim, and warning against abandoning his aid. Al-Harith said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, who said: Sulayman said: Waqqas ibn Rabi'ah narrated to us that al-Mustawrid narrated to them that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats a meal through a Muslim man, Allah will feed him the like of it from the boiling water of Hell; whoever clothes himself with a garment through a Muslim man, Allah, Exalted, will clothe him the like of it from Hell; and whoever stands with a Muslim man in a stand of showing off, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will stand him in a stand of showing off on the Day of Resurrection."
"3257","Chapter: Deterrence from imitating others. Abu Ya'la said: Sa'id ibn Abi al-Rabi' al-Samman narrated to us, Anbasah narrated to us, Hammad, freedman of Umayyah, narrated to us, from Janah, freedman of al-Walid, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of the youth is he who imitates your elders, and the worst of your elders is he who imitates your youth."
"3258","Chapter: Prohibition of praising the sinner. Abu Ya'la said: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Saminah al-Baghdadi narrated to us, al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Sabiq narrated to us, from Abu Khalaf, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, becomes angry when the sinner is praised."
"3259","He said: And Rabah ibn al-Jarrah narrated to me, from Sabiq, from Abu Khalaf, and he mentioned similarly, adding: And the Throne shook. Abu Ya'la said: This is from my memory."
"3260","Chapter: Prohibition of faulting people. Al-Harith said: Al-Khalil ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Mujalid narrated to us, from Amir, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas missed a rak'ah of the dawn prayer, so he stood making it up. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, and the people sat around him. When Thabit ibn Qays finished prayer, he came to a man and said: Make room for me, so he made room for him. Then he came to a second and said: Make room for me, so he made room for him. Then he came to a third and said: Make room for me, and he said: Behind you is room; why do you step over people? He looked at his face and said: O son of so-and-so woman. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard it and said: Who is the one who just reproached the man for his mother? They fell silent. Then he said a second time: Who is the one who just reproached the man for his mother? Thabit stood and said: I missed a rak'ah, and in my ear is deafness, and I desired to be near you, and the people sat around you. He mentioned the story. He said: So I reproached him for a mother from the pre-Islamic time, other women being better than her. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Thabit ibn Qays, raise your head above this crowd; among them are the black, the white, and the red; you are no better than these except through God-fearing. He said: After that day I never reproached anyone."
"3261","Chapter: Prohibition of pursuing faults. Abu Ya'la said: Ibrahim ibn Dinar narrated to us, Mus'ab ibn Sallam narrated to us, from Hamzah al-Zayyat, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us until he made the secluded maidens in their houses hear, or he said in their chambers, and he said: O company of those who believed with their tongues while faith did not enter their hearts, do not backbite the Muslims, nor pursue their faults; for whoever pursues his brother's fault, Allah will pursue his fault, and whomever Allah pursues for his fault will disgrace him in the midst of his house."
"3262","Abd said: Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to us, Khalid ibn Ilyas narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man sees a fault of his brother and conceals it for him except that Allah will admit him to Paradise."
"3263","Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ubayd Allah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Muslim is the mirror of the Muslim; when he sees something in him, let him remove it."
"3264","Chapter: Prohibition of pre-Islamic claims, boasting, and reproaching by fathers. Abu Ya'la said: Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Abu Hafs al-Abbar informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had two freedmen: an Abyssinian and a Nabatean. They insulted each other while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) listened. One of them said to his companion: O Nabatean, and the other said: O Abyssinian. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not say this; you are only two men among the companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3265","Chapter: Blame of envy. The hadith of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, preceded in the Hudud. Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from al-Hasan, or from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Envy almost precedes destiny, and poverty almost becomes disbelief."
"3266","Chapter: Manners of sitting at the door of the house. Abu Bakr said: Uqbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Musa ibn Muhammad, my father narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade spreading bedding at the doors of houses, and he said: Move it away from the door somewhat."
"3267","Chapter: Honoring the neighbor. The hadith of Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her: Do not harm your neighbor, preceded in the chapter of sleeping manners. Musaddad said: Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated to us, who said: I heard Sufyan say: When you buy something you do not wish to share with your neighbor, conceal it."
"3268","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, Abu Mahal narrated to me, who said: from an old woman, from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said, he said: When your neighbor's young boy enters upon you, place something in his hand, for it brings affection."
"3269","Abu Bakr said: Al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, Bashir ibn Salman narrated to us, from Mujahid, who said: We were sitting with Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoining the neighbor until we thought, or we saw, that he would make him an heir."
"3270","Abd said: Ya'la, that is Ibn Ubayd, narrated to us, from Abu Bakr, that is Ibn Mubashshir, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man from al-Awali came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Jibril, peace be upon him, were praying where funeral prayers are performed. When he finished, the man said: O Messenger of Allah, who is this I saw with you? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have you seen him? He said: Yes. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have seen much good; this is Jibril, peace be upon him. He kept enjoining me regarding the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir."
"3271","Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Abu Nasr narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: Whoever is asked by his neighbor to support upon his wall, let him do so."
"3272","Al-Harith said: Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Hunayn ibn Abi Hakim, from Irak ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my neighbor so-and-so harms me. He said: Restrain your harm from him and be patient over his harm. Only a short while passed until he came and said: O Messenger of Allah, my neighbor so-and-so who used to harm me has died. He said: He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Time suffices as an admonisher, and death suffices as a separator."
"3273","Abu Ya'la said: Al-Mughirah ibn Ma'mar Abu al-Fadl al-Basri narrated to us, Mas'adah ibn al-Yasa' narrated to us, from Bahz, from his father, from his grandfather, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have two neighbors; to which of them shall I give? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The nearer of the two."
"3274","Abu Musa and al-Qawariri narrated to us, separating them, both saying: Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from his father, from Abayah ibn Rifa'ah, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A man does not eat his fill while his neighbor goes without."
"3275","Abu Musa narrated to us, Abbad ibn Musa Abu Ayyub narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Muhammad ibn Maslamah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I passed by and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on al-Safa placing his cheek upon the cheek of a man, so he left. It was not long before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called me, and I hastened to him. He said: O Muhammad ibn Maslamah, what prevented you from greeting? I said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw you do with this man something you did with none of the people, so I disliked interrupting your talk. Who was that, O Messenger of Allah? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril. Know that had you greeted, we would have returned upon you. He said: And what did he say to you, O Messenger of Allah? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He kept enjoining me regarding the neighbor until I expected he would command me to make him an heir."
"3276","Muhammad ibn Jami' al-Attar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Abi al-Janub narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The right of the neighbor is forty cubits, like this, like this, like this, and like this, to the right, to the left, in front, and behind."
"3277","Chapter: Command to show affection to brothers. Al-Harith said: Dawud ibn Rashid narrated to us, Umar Abu Hafs narrated to us, from Abu Muhammad al-Ansari, from Yazid, from Abu Humayd al-Sa'idi, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Render affection to your beloved, for it is more lasting."
"3278","Abu Ya'la said: Abdullah ibn Salamah narrated to us, Imran ibn Khalid al-Khuza'i narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to make brotherhood between two of his Companions, and the night would grow long upon one of them until he met his brother, meeting him with affection and gentleness, saying: How were you after me? As for the generality, three days would not pass upon one of them without knowing his brother's state."
"3279","Abu Bakr said: Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Imran al-Qasir, Sa'id ibn Sulayman informed me, from Yazid ibn Nu'amah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man takes another man as a brother, let him ask him about his name, his father's name, and who he is, for it is more conducive to affection."
"3280","Chapter: Mixing with people. Al-Harith said: Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from one of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The believer who mixes with people and bears their harm patiently has greater reward than the believer who does not mix with people nor bear their harm patiently."
"3281","Abu Bakr said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from a man among the Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), may Allah be pleased with him, raised to the Prophet, similarly."
"3282","Chapter: The best of matters is the middle. Abu Ya'la said: Ibrahim narrated to us, from Isma'il, Abd al-Samad ibn Ma'qil narrated to us, that he heard Wahb say: Everything has two ends and a middle; when one end is held, the other inclines, and when the middle is held, the two ends are balanced. And he said: Upon you is the middle course in things."
"3283","Chapter: Love and brotherhood. Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Love your beloved moderately, perhaps he will be your hated one someday; and hate your hated one moderately, perhaps he will be your beloved someday."
"3284","Mu'tamir narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from al-Hasan, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: No Muslim increases in brotherhood for Allah, Exalted, except that he is raised a degree thereby."
"3285","Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Balj, from Amr ibn Maymun, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you loves a servant, let him inform him, for he will find for him the like of what he finds. Mursal."
"3286","Abu Ya'la said: Muhammad ibn Qudamah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Yahya, from Mujahid, who said: A man passed by Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, and said: This man loves me. They said: And how do you know, O Ibn Abbas? He, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Because I love him."
"3287","Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Abu Isma'il al-Abdi, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever takes a new brother in Islam, Allah, Exalted, raises him a degree in Paradise thereby; and no two servants love each other for Allah, Exalted, then are separated except due to a sin one of them commits; and no two servants love each other for Allah, Exalted, except that the better of them with Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is the one with stronger love for his companion."
"3288","Abu Bakr said: Yahya ibn Ya'la narrated to us, from Humayd, that is al-A'raj, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Those who love one another are upon a pillar of red ruby, overlooking the people of this world. He said: The people of Paradise will say: Come out with us to look at those who love one another for Allah, Mighty and Majestic. He said: They will come out and look at them, their faces like the night of the full moon, written on their foreheads: These are those who love one another for Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"3289","Abu Ya'la said: Ahmad ibn Hatim narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Humayd, with it, adding: Upon the top of the pillar are seventy thousand chambers; their beauty shines upon the people of Paradise as the sun shines upon the people of this world. And in it: Upon them are green garments of sundus."
"3290","Abd said: Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, from Musa ibn Wardan, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise there are pillars of ruby, upon them chambers of chrysolite with open doors, shining as the brilliant star shines. We said: O Messenger of Allah, who will dwell in them? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Those who love one another for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, those who sit together for Allah, Exalted, and those who show affection for Allah, Majestic is His majesty."
"3291","Abu Ya'la said: Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fudalah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No two men ever love each other except that the better of them is the one with stronger love for his companion."
"3292","Chapter: Employing free men, not counted as pride. Ibn Abi Umar said: Al-Muqri narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from al-Qasim, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat, Abdullah would remove his sandals from his feet and place them in his arms; when he stood, he would put them on him, and walk with the staff before him until he entered the chamber."
"3293","Chapter: Competing in serving the elder. Abu Ya'la said: Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim, that is Abu Yusuf the judge, narrated to us, Abu Hanifah narrated to us, from al-Haytham, meaning Ibn Habib, who said: Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I have not lied since I became Muslim except one lie. I used to saddle for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a saddler from Ta'if came and said: Which saddle is most pleasing to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I said: The Ta'ifi with shoulder pads. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to dislike it. When he saddled it and it was brought, he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who saddled this for us? I said: So-and-so whom you brought from Ta'if saddled it for you. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Return the mount to Ibn Mas'ud."
"3294","Chapter: Warning against leaving circumcision. Abu Bakr said: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Umm al-Aswad, from Munyah, from her grandfather Abu Barzah al-Aslami, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: They asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about an uncircumcised man performing pilgrimage to the House of Allah, Exalted? He said: No; Allah forbade me from that until he is circumcised."
"3295","Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, with this. This chain is hasan, and the name of Munyah's father is Ubayd ibn Abi Barzah; al-Abbas al-Asfati named her, from Ibn Yunus."
"3296","Chapter: Intellect and its virtue. Al-Harith ibn Abi Usamah said: Abu al-Fadl narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Khulayd ibn Da'laj, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They do good, but they are given their rewards according to their intellects. This is mursal, and its chain is also weak."
"3297","Al-Harith ibn Abi Usamah said: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, Maysarah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, who said: Umar, Abu Hurayrah, and Ubayy ibn Ka'b entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, who is the most knowledgeable of people? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The intelligent. They said: Then who is the most worshipful of people? He said: The intelligent. They said: Then who is the best of people? He said: The intelligent. They said: O Messenger of Allah, is not the intelligent one whose manliness is complete, whose eloquence is manifest, whose station is great? He said: All that is but the enjoyment of worldly life; rather the intelligent is the God-fearing, even if in this world he is lowly, distant, base."
"3298","Dawud narrated to us, Muqatil ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man attains with good character the rank of the fasting, devoutly obedient person; and a man's good character is not complete until his intellect is complete; then his trustworthiness and faith are complete: he obeys his Lord and disobeys his enemy Iblis."
"3299","Dawud narrated to us, Adi ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People are reckoned according to their intellects."
"3300","Dawud narrated to us, Maysarah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Amrah, from Aishah, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, by what do people excel in this world? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By intellect. I said: Then in the Hereafter? He said: By intellect. She said: I said: They are only rewarded for their deeds. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And did they act except according to what Allah, Exalted, gave them of intellect? According to what they were given of intellect were their deeds, and according to what they did they will be rewarded."
"3301","Dawud narrated to us, from Maysarah, from Ghalib, from Ibn Hunayn, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, raising it to the Prophet: Everything has a tool and provision, and the tool and provision of the believer is intellect; the support of the believer is intellect. Everything has a goal, and the goal of worship is intellect. Every people has a shepherd, and the shepherd of worshipers is intellect. Every merchant has goods, and the goods of strivers is intellect. Every household has a guardian, and the guardian of the houses of the truthful is intellect. Every ruin has a building, and the building of the Hereafter is intellect. Every matter has an outcome attributed to it and remembered by it, and the outcome of the truthful attributed to them and remembered by them is intellect. Every group has a tent they resort to, and the tent of believers is intellect."
"3302","Dawud narrated to us, Nasr ibn Tarif narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man's support is his intellect, and there is no religion for one without intellect."
"3303","Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, Abbad narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: O people, understand from your Lord, and humble yourselves through intellect in what you are commanded and what you are forbidden; know that He warns you before your Lord. Know that the intelligent is he who obeys Allah, Exalted, even if unsightly in appearance, lowly in rank, base in station, shabby in form; and the ignorant is he who disobeys Allah, even if beautiful in appearance, noble in station, fine in form, eloquent and fluent. Apes and pigs understand from Allah, Exalted, better than one who disobeys Him. Do not be deluded by the glorification of worldly people toward you, for tomorrow you will be among the losers."
"3304","Dawud narrated to us, Maysarah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man may have good intellect and many sins. He said: There is no human except that he has faults and sins he commits; whoever has intellect as his nature and certainty as his disposition, sins will not harm him. It was said: And how is that, O Messenger of Allah? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Because whenever he errs, he soon remedies it with repentance and regret for what he did, wiping away his sins, leaving him merit by which he enters Paradise."
"3305","Dawud narrated to us, Maysarah narrated to us, from Hanzalah ibn Wada'ah, from al-Bara ibn Azib, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The angels strove and exerted themselves in obeying Allah through intellect, and the believers strove and exerted themselves in obeying Allah according to their intellects; the most knowledgeable of them in obeying Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is the most abundant of them in intellect."
"3306","Dawud narrated to us, Maysarah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Qatadah, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what of the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: Which of you is best in deed, what did He mean by it? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Which of you is best in intellect. Then he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most complete of you in intellect is the most fearful of Allah, and the best of you in regard for what is commanded and forbidden, even if the least of you in voluntary deeds."
"3307","Dawud narrated to us, Maysarah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Two men head to the mosque and pray, then one leaves with his prayer weightier than Uhud, while the other leaves with his prayer not equaling a speck's weight. Abu Humayd al-Sa'idi, may Allah be pleased with him, said: And how can that be? He said: When one is better in intellect. He said: And how is that? He said: When he is more wary of Allah's prohibitions and keener to hasten to good, even if less in voluntary deeds."
"3308","Dawud narrated to us, Abbad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said to Tamim al-Dari, may Allah be pleased with him: What is eminence among you? He said: Intellect. He said: You spoke the truth; I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as I asked you, and he said as you said. Then he said: I asked Jibril, peace be upon him: What is eminence among people? He said: Intellect."
"3309","Dawud narrated to us, Abbad narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Everything has a support, and the support of the believer is his intellect; according to his intellect is his worship of his Lord. Have you not heard the saying of the wicked at his regret: Had we listened or reasoned, we would not have been among the companions of the Blaze."
"3310","Dawud narrated to us, Abbad narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Consult the intelligent and you will be guided; do not disobey him lest you regret."
"3311","Dawud narrated to us, Maysarah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Sa'id, that Mu'awiyah, may Allah be pleased with them both, addressed them and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The best of my companions and their choicest are their most God-fearing. Abu Sa'id said: Their most God-fearing are their most intelligent; thus the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said."
"3312","Dawud narrated to us, Maysarah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Jaban, from Luqman ibn Amir, who said: Abu al-Darda, may Allah be pleased with him, said, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The ignorant reveals only disgrace, even if clever and refined before people; and the intelligent reveals only merit, even if faulty and lowly before people."
"3313","Dawud narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Kulayb ibn Wa'il, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He recited: Blessed is He in Whose Hand is dominion, up to His saying: That He may test you, which of you is best in deed. He said: Which of you is best in intellect, most wary of Allah's prohibitions, and quickest in obeying Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"3314","Dawud narrated to us, Abbad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: How many an intelligent one about Allah's command, lowly before people and unsightly in appearance, will be saved tomorrow; and how many an eloquent-tongued, handsome, well-dressed one will perish tomorrow at the Resurrection."
"3315","Dawud narrated to us, Abbad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Abu Sa'id, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah, Exalted, divided intellect into three parts: whoever has them, his intellect is complete, and whoever lacks them has no intellect: good knowledge of Allah, Exalted, good obedience to Him, and good patience upon His command."
"3316","Dawud narrated to us, Attab ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from al-Rabi' ibn Lut, from his father, from his grandfather, from al-Bara ibn Azib, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: Questions became many before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: O people, every path has a mount, a pledge, and a clear proof; and the firmest of people in mount, the best in guidance and knowledge of soundness, is the best of them in intellect."
"3317","Dawud narrated to us, Abbad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Tawus, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from the raid of Uhud, he heard people saying: So-and-so was braver than so-and-so, so-and-so was bolder than so-and-so, and so-and-so endured what others did not, and the like, praising them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for this, you have no knowledge of it. They said: And how is that, O Messenger of Allah? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All of them fought according to what Allah apportioned them of intellect, and their victory and intention were according to their intellects; some of them were struck upon various stations. When the Day of Resurrection comes, they will share their stations according to their intentions and intellects."
"3318","Dawud narrated to us, Sallam Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us, from Musa ibn Jaban, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: People praised a man before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until they exceeded in praise of good traits. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How is the man's intellect? They said: O Messenger of Allah, we tell you of his striving in worship and kinds of good, and you ask us about his intellect? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The fool through his folly attains greater evil than the wickedness of the wicked; servants are raised tomorrow in ranks and attain nearness to their Lord according to their intellects."
"3319","And with this chain to Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Ibn Salam came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I will ask you about traits Allah informed none about except Musa ibn Imran; if you know them, then so it is, otherwise it is something Allah singled Musa ibn Imran, peace be upon him, with. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Ibn Salam, if you wish ask me, and if you wish I shall tell you. He said: Tell me. He said: The near angels did not encompass the creation of the Throne, nor have knowledge of it, nor its bearers who carry it. When Allah created the heavens and the earth, the angels said: Our Lord, did You create a creation greater than the heavens and the earth? He said: Yes, the seas. They said: Did You create a creation greater than the seas? He said: Yes, the Throne. He said: Did You create a creation greater than the Throne? He said: Yes, intellect. They said: Our Lord, what is the extent of intellect and its creation? He said: Far from it; its knowledge cannot be encompassed. He said: Do you have knowledge of the number of sand? They said: No. He said: I created intellect in various kinds like the number of sand; some people were given one grain of it, some two, three, four, some were given a faraq, some were given a wasaq, some were given two wasaqs, and some were given more than that up to manifold as Allah wills. Ibn Salam, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Then who are those, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The workers in obeying Allah, Exalted, according to their deeds, striving, and certainty; the light Allah, Exalted, placed in their hearts and their understanding thereof is all according to what He gave them. According to that, the worker among them works and rises in ranks. Ibn Salam, may Allah be pleased with him, said: By Him Who sent you with guidance and the religion of truth, I do not omit a single letter of what I found in the Torah; Musa, peace be upon him, was the first to describe this description, and you are the second. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You spoke the truth, O Ibn Salam."
"3320","Dawud narrated to us, Abbad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: No man earned anything better than intellect guiding its owner to guidance and turning him from ruin; a servant's faith is not complete, nor his religion upright, until his intellect is complete."
"3321","Dawud narrated to us, Maysarah narrated to us, from al-Mughirah ibn Qays, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, to what do people end on the Day of Resurrection? He said: To their deeds: whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it. He said: I said: Which of them is best in deeds? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of them in intellect. I said: This is in this world; which of them is best in the Hereafter? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of them in intellect; intellect is the master of deeds in both abodes together."
"3322","Dawud narrated to us, Hasan narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu al-Darda, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, what of a man who stands the night, fasts the day, performs pilgrimage and umrah, fights in the way of Allah, Exalted, visits the sick, joins kinship, follows funerals, and honors the guest, until he counted these ten traits; what is his station with Allah, Exalted, on the Day of Resurrection? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: His reward on the Day of Resurrection in all that is according to his intellect."
"3323","Dawud narrated to us, Maysarah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Jaban, from Luqman ibn Amir, from Abu al-Darda, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Uwaymir, increase in intellect and you will increase in nearness to your Lord. He said: I said: May my father and mother be ransomed for you, O Messenger of Allah, and how may I attain that? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Avoid Allah's prohibitions, Mighty and Majestic, and perform Allah's obligations, Exalted, and you will be intelligent; and do voluntary good deeds, and you will increase thereby in the present world in elevation and honor, and attain thereby from your Lord nearness and might."
"3324","Dawud narrated to us, Abbad narrated to us, from Abd al-Wahhab ibn Mujahid, from his father, who said: I said to Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both: Which pilgrims of Allah's House are best and greatest in reward? He, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Whoever combines three traits: a sincere intention, abundant intellect, and spending from lawful means. That was mentioned to Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, and he said: He spoke the truth. I said: When his intention is sincere and his spending is from lawful, what does little intellect harm him? He said: O Abu al-Hajjaj, you ask me about what I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about. He said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, a servant does not obey his Lord with anything, nor jihad, nor anything of kinds of righteousness, if he does not understand it; were an ignorant one with his intellect to surpass the strivers in worship, what he corrupts would be more than what he reforms."
"3325","Dawud narrated to us, Nasr ibn Tarif narrated to us, from Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir, from Abu Wa'il, from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah, who said: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, went out one day, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met him. He said to him: What brought you, O Messenger of Allah? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Intellect. He said: With what were you commanded? He said: With intellect. He said: Then with what will people be recompensed on the Day of Resurrection? He said: With intellect. He said: Then how may we attain intellect? He said: Intellect has no limit; but whoever makes lawful Allah's lawful and unlawful His unlawful is called intelligent. If he strives in worship and is generous in the ranks of good, with no share of intellect guiding him to follow Allah's command, Exalted, and avoid what He forbade, those are the greatest losers whose striving strayed in worldly life while they think they do well."
"3326","Dawud narrated to us, Maysarah narrated to us, from Ghalib al-Jazari, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, raising it to the Prophet, who said: The trait of the intelligent is that he forbears toward one ignorant toward him, pardons one who wronged him, humbles himself to one below him, vies with one above him in seeking righteousness; when he wishes to speak he reflects: if good, he speaks and gains, if evil, he is silent and safe; when trial appears he seeks protection with Allah and holds his hand and tongue; when he sees a merit he seizes it; modesty never leaves him, greed never appears from him. Those are ten traits by which the intelligent is known. He said: And the trait of the ignorant is that he wrongs whoever mixes with him, follows whoever is below him, exalts himself over whoever is above him; his speech is without reflection: if he speaks he sins, if he is silent he errs; when trial appears he hastens to it and it destroys him; when he sees a merit he turns from it and is slow toward it; he fears not his old sins, nor restrains himself in the rest of his life from sins, lax toward righteousness, slow toward it, unconcerned for what he missed or wasted thereof. Ten traits of the ignorant deprived of intellect."
"3327","Chapter: Dislike of sitting in the house. Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Isma'il, Qays narrated to me, from Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, I heard him say: The least blame upon a man is to sit in his house. Sahih, stopped."
"3328","Chapter: Permissibility of naming with prophets' names, and what came about disliking it. Ishaq said: Waki' informed us, Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from his father, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, gathered every boy named with a prophet's name, entered them into a house, and wanted to change their names; their fathers testified that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named them. He said: And my father Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm was among them. This chain is hasan."
"3329","Al-Tayalisi said: al-Hakam ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You name them Muhammad, then you curse them."
"3330","Abu Ya'la said: Abu Musa narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us with this."
"3331","Abd said: Abu al-Walid narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, with it."
"3332","Al-Harith said: Isma'il ibn Abi Isma'il narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Nadr ibn Shafiyy, who said, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever has three children born and names none of them Muhammad has been ignorant."
"3333","Abu Bakr said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, freedman of Talhah's family, from Isa ibn Talhah, who said: The foster mother of Muhammad ibn Talhah narrated to me, who said: When Muhammad ibn Talhah, may Allah be pleased with him, was born, we brought him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: What did you name him? We said: Muhammad. He said: This is my name, and his kunyah is Abu al-Qasim."
"3334","Chapter: Dislike of naming with tyrants' names, and changing the name to what is better. Al-Harith said: Isma'il ibn Abi Isma'il narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyib, who said: A boy was born to the brother of Umm Salamah, and they named him al-Walid. They entered with him upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Did you name him? They said: Yes, they named him al-Walid. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hush, hush; his name is Abd al-Rahman. Did you name him with the name of your Pharaohs? There will be in my nation a man called al-Walid, more severe upon my nation than Pharaoh upon his people. Abd al-Rahman said: I said to him: Which al-Walid is he? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If al-Walid ibn Yazid is made caliph, otherwise he is al-Walid ibn Abd al-Malik."
"3335","Ibn Abi Umar said: Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, had a slave-girl with a foreign name, so Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, named her Jamilah. Umar said: Between me and you is the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). We came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to her: You are Jamilah. Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Take it despite yourself."
"3336","Abu Ya'la said: Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Abu Sa'id narrated, Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Abza narrated, he said: my mother narrated to me, from her father: that he was present at the spoils of Hunayn with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his name was Ghurab (Crow), so the Messenger of Allah named him Muslim."
"3337","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abdah narrated, from Hisham, from his father, from A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a land called Ghabarah, and said: It is Khadirah."
"3338","Chapter: The most beloved names to Allah the Exalted (76). Abu Ya'la said: Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated, from Isma'il ibn Muslim, from al-Hasan, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most beloved names to Allah the Mighty and Majestic are Abdullah and Abdurrahman. It has a witness from the hadith of Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) in Muslim."
"3339","Chapter: Allusion regarding asking about a need, whether it was fulfilled or not (77). Ibn Abi Shaybah said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Rabi'ah ibn al-Harith ibn Abdulmuttalib, who said: My father sent me, and al-Abbas sent his son al-Fadl (may Allah be pleased with them) to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)... then he mentioned the hadith, he said: When we came to them they said: What is behind you, As'ad or Sa'id?"
"3340","Chapter: Gentle dealing (78). Al-Harith said: al-Khalil ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Hisham narrated, from Asim, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Safwan ibn Assal (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, when a man came forward; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at him he said: Evil brother of the tribe, or evil man; when he drew near him he brought his sitting place close, and when he stood and left they said: O Messenger of Allah, when you saw him you said: Evil brother of the tribe or evil man, then you brought his sitting place close. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is a hypocrite, I deal with him gently because of his hypocrisy, and I fear he may corrupt others against me."
"3341","Chapter: Manners of sitting and sleeping (79). Al-Harith said: Yazid narrated to us, Hammad narrated, from Abdulmalik ibn Umayr, from Abu Shaybah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you enters among people and a place is made wide for him, let him sit, for it is only an honor from Allah the Mighty and Majestic by which his Muslim brother has honored him; if no place is made wide for him, let him look at the widest place and sit in it."
"3342","Mus'ab az-Zubayri narrated to us, ad-Darawardi narrated, from Mus'ab ibn Thabit, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of sittings are the widest. Al-Bazzar said: We do not know it from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) except from this route."
"3343","He said: And Abdulaziz ibn Aban narrated to us, Hisham narrated, from a man, from Yahya ibn Ya'mar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a sitting place on a road and said: Beware of the road, for it is the path of the Fire and Satan; then he went on until they thought it was a firm resolve, then he came back and said: Except that you fulfill the right of the road. They said: What is the right of the road? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That you lower your gazes, guide the lost, and return the greeting of peace."
"3344","And Musaddad said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad that he used to dislike a man sleeping on his stomach, and a woman lying on her back. Halted (mawquf), sahih."
"3345","And Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Abu al-Ala al-Hasan ibn Sawwar narrated to us, al-Layth narrated. Al-Harith said: And Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, al-Layth narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu Nadr who said: Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) was complaining of his leg; his brother entered upon him while he had placed one of his legs over the other as he reclined, so he struck his painful leg with his hand, causing him pain. He said: You have pained me, did you not know my leg is painful? He said: Yes. He said: What made you do that? He said: Did you not hear that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that? I say: His brother's name is Qatadah ibn Nu'man."
"3346","Chapter: Prohibition of sleeping on a roof that has no parapet (80). Ahmad ibn Mani' said: And Abu Ahmad az-Zubayri narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated, from Imran ibn Muslim ibn Rabah, from Ali ibn Umarah who said: A bed was spread for Abu Ayyub al-Ansari on an open roof, and during the night he ordered it to be taken down, and said: I almost spent the night with no protection for me."
"3347","And al-Harith said: al-Khalil ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Habib ibn Shahid narrated, from al-Hasan, from Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever spends the night on a roof that is not enclosed is absolved of protection, whoever shoots at night is absolved of protection, and whoever rides the sea when it is agitated is absolved of protection."
"3348","Chapter: Deliberation and gentleness (81). Abu Bakr said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us. And Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us. And al-Harith said: Abu Nadr narrated to us, they said: al-Layth narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Sinan ibn Sa'd, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Deliberation is from Allah the Exalted, and haste is from Satan; there is nothing with more excuses than Allah the Mighty and Majestic, and there is nothing more beloved to Allah the Exalted than praise."
"3349","And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us with this."
"3350","And Abu Bakr said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Sa'd ibn Sa'id narrated, from az-Zuhri, from a man of Bali, who said: I entered with my father upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he spoke to him privately apart from me. I said: O father, what did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say to you? He said: He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: When you intend a matter, stick to deliberation until Allah brings you a way out of your matter."
"3351","And Abu Ya'la said: Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ad-Dawraqi narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated, and he said at its end: until Allah brings you relief in your matter."
"3352","And al-Harith said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated, from Sa'd ibn Sa'id similar to it."
"3353","Chapter: Example of the righteous companion (82). Ishaq said: al-Makhzumi informed us, Abdulwahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated, from Khaythamah, who said: Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The example of the righteous companion is like the owner of musk; if he does not give you, his scent reaches you; and the example of the evil companion is like the owner of the bellows; if he does not burn your clothes his scent reaches you or his foul smell harms you. This chain has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"3354","And Abd said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Hassan narrated, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, which of our companions is best? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One whose seeing reminds you of Allah, whose speech increases your deeds, and whose action reminds you of the Hereafter."
"3355","And Abu Ya'la said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ali ibn Hashim narrated to us, Mubarak narrated with it."
"3356","Chapter: Fairness to slaves, and what is acquired of them and of animals (83). Al-Harith said: al-Khalil ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Awf narrated, from al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Set right your dwellings, make one head two heads, and frighten vermin before they frighten you. Al-Khalil ibn Zakariyya said: Your dwellings are your houses; one head two heads means when he wants to buy a slave for ten thousand, let him buy two; vermin are snakes."
"3357","And Musaddad said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Abu Ammar, from Abu Maysarah Amr ibn Shurahbil (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sheep are blessing, camels are honor for their people, good is tied in the forelocks of horses, and the slave is your brother, so do good to him; if you see him overpowered, help him. Mursal."
"3358","And al-Harith said: al-Khalil ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Awn narrated, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sheep are blessing, and camels are honor for their people."
"3359","And Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Rishdin narrated, from Abu Abdullah, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded the rich to take sheep, and commanded the poor to take chickens."
"3360","And Abu Ya'la said: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Bara (may Allah be pleased with him), raised once and halted another time, who said: Sheep are blessing."
"3361","And al-Humaydi said: Mahdi narrated to us, from Wasil, from Hilal, from Abu Sinan, freedman of Banu Hashim, who said: It reached us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the worst of your slaves are the Sudanese; if hungry they steal, and if full they commit adultery."
"3362","Chapter: Wiping the head of a small child and mercy to the orphan (84). Abu Ya'la said: Abu Ma'mar narrated to us, Atwan narrated, from Jamrah al-Hanzaliyyah, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the camels of charity, and he wiped my head and supplicated good for me. Abu Ma'mar said: In this hadith is wiping the head of a woman, because she does not come with charity camels except grown. I say: Restriction is prevented, so there is no preventer that she comes while discerning, with care and herding upon others from the servants, and perhaps her father intended by sending her that blessing reach her through the supplication of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he had no male child, so his aim was achieved."
"3363","Chapter: Vastness of Allah's mercy and encouragement of mercy (85). Abd said: Abdullah ibn Bakr as-Sahmi narrated to us, Fa'id Abu al-Warqa narrated, from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa al-Aslami (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I went out to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while Abu Bakr and Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) were sitting; a small boy was weeping, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Umar (may Allah be pleased with him): Join the boy to you, for he is lost. So Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) joined him to himself. While we were sitting, a woman came wailing, I think, saying: O my son, and weeping. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Call the woman, for she is the mother of the boy, and she is uncovering her head with no veil upon it, in grief for her son. She came until she took the boy from the lap of Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) while weeping, the boy in her lap. She turned, and when she saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) she said: O my shame, do I not see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said at that: Do you see this one merciful to her child? His companions (may Allah be pleased with them) said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), sufficient is this mercy. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, Allah the Exalted is more merciful to the believers than this one to her child."
"3364","And al-Harith said: Abdurrahman ibn Waqid narrated to us, Hassan ibn Ibrahim al-Kirmani narrated, Sa'id ibn Masruq narrated, from Abu Amr ash-Shaybani, from a man from the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, when some of them took a sparrow chick; the sparrow began falling upon their saddles, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that its chick be returned to it, then he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is more merciful to His servant than this sparrow to its chick."
"3365","And Abu Ya'la said: Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abdurrahman ibn Muhammad narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Sinan, from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, Allah does not place His mercy except upon one who is merciful. They said: O Messenger of Allah, all of us show mercy. He said: Not the mercy of one of you alone, until he shows mercy to people all together."
"3366","And al-Harith said: Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Abu Azhar who said: A man passed with two bird chicks before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while their father hovered over them, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You took these two chicks while their father hovers over them; why did you not leave him one of them so his eye would be comforted by it."
"3367","Abdurrahim ibn Waqid narrated to us, Abdulghafur ibn Abdulaziz narrated, Abdulaziz ibn Sa'id al-Ansari narrated, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Exalted indeed shows mercy to His believing servant on the Day of Resurrection with the mercy of a sparrow."
"3368","Chapter: Kindness to slaves (86). Ishaq said: Baqiyyah ibn Walid informed us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam al-Ghassani, from Abu Mujashi' al-Azdi, from Umar ibn Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever buys any servants and their character does not agree with his character, let him sell and buy until their character agrees with his character, for people are of characters; and do not punish the servant of Allah."
"3369","Isa ibn Yunus informed us, from Abu Bakr with this chain similar to it, and he did not raise it."
"3370","And Abu Ya'la said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Musa narrated, Ibn Mubarak narrated, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from Qasim, from Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Fear Allah, fear Allah regarding those whom your right hands possess; fill their stomachs, clothe their backs, and soften speech to them."
"3371","And Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn Musa informed us, from Farqad, from Murrah at-Tayyib, from Abu Bakr as-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The first to enter Paradise is the slave, when he obeys Allah the Exalted and obeys his master."
"3372","Abbad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Hilal narrated, a trustworthy companion of ours narrated, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gabriel (peace be upon him) kept advising me regarding the slave until I thought he would set a limit; when they reach it they are freed."
"3373","And Abd ibn Humayd said: Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated, from Humayd ibn Hani, who said: Amr ibn Hurayth (may Allah be pleased with him) informed me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever you lighten of your servant's work is reward for you in your scales."
"3374","And Abu Bakr said: Muhammad ibn Hasan narrated to us, Abu Jumay' al-Hujaymi narrated, from Thabit, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave Ali and Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with them both) a boy servant, and said: Do good to him, for I saw him praying."
"3375","And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this."
"3376","Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated, from Mughirah ibn Muslim Abu Salamah, from Farqad as-Sabakhi, from Murrah at-Tayyib, from Abu Bakr as-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding slaves: Honor them as you honor your children, feed them from what you eat, and clothe them from what you wear."
"3377","Chapter: Manners of messengers (87). Ibn Abi Umar said: ath-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, who said: Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: I was with the Commander of the Believers Umar (may Allah be pleased with him); he said: Go and tell me who that is? He (may Allah be pleased with him) when he sent a man for a need would say: When you return, tell me what I sent you for and what is answered to me. So I said: You ordered me to know who that is, and he is Suhayb (may Allah be pleased with him) with him a slave girl. He (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Let him join us, even if a slave girl is with him... then he mentioned the hadith."
"3378","Chapter: Honoring the elder (88). Musaddad said: Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Abu Asim ath-Thaqafi, from ash-Sha'bi who said: Jarir ibn Yazid ibn Jarir came to him, so he threw a cushion for him while elders were with him; he was asked about that, so he said: It reached me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the noble of a people comes to you, honor him."
"3379","Chapter: Rebuke against honoring polytheists (89). Ishaq said: Baqiyyah ibn Walid informed us, Muhammad al-Qushayri narrated to me, from Abu Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade shaking hands with polytheists, giving them kunyas, or welcoming them."
"3380","Chapter: Honoring the visitor (91). Al-Harith said: Dawud narrated to us, Hammad narrated, from Bishr ibn Harb, who said: We were with Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) one day when suddenly Abdullah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) entered; I saw him changed, gloomy and sad, with traces of dust upon him, so Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) called for water for him and he performed ablution."
"3381","And Abu Ya'la said: Ubaydullah al-Qawariri narrated to us, Ulaylah bint Kumayt narrated to us, my mother Aminah narrated to me, that Amatullah bint Razinah narrated to her, from her mother Razinah, freedwoman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Sawdah the Yemeni came to visit A'ishah while Hafsah bint Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) was with her. Sawdah (may Allah be pleased with her) came in a fine appearance, wearing a cloak of Yemeni cloth and likewise a veil, with two spots like lentils of aloes and saffron at her temples. Ulaylah said: I saw women adorning with it. Hafsah said to A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her): O Mother of the Believers, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will come and see us unkempt while this one shines among us. She (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Fear Allah, O Hafsah, fear Allah, O Hafsah. She said: I will spoil her adornment. She (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Do so. Sawdah had heaviness in her ear, so Hafsah said to her: O Sawdah, the one-eyed has come out. She was seized with severe fright and began trembling. She said: Where shall I hide? She said: To the tent, a tent of theirs of palm leaves in which they cooked. She went and hid, in it were pots and cobwebs. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came while they both laughed, unable to speak from laughter. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is this laughter? Three times. They pointed with their hands to the tent. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went, and there was Sawdah trembling. He said to her: O Sawdah, what is with you? She said: O Messenger of Allah, the one-eyed has come out. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has not come out, but he will surely come out. Then he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and brought her out, brushing off her dust and cobwebs."
"3382","Chapter: Description of the heart of the son of Adam (93). Ishaq said: Baqiyyah ibn Walid informed us, Buhayr ibn Sa'id narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Abu Ubaydah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The heart of the son of Adam is like a sparrow, turning seven times a day. Its chain is hasan, but it is disconnected."
"3383","Chapter: Love of children (94). Abu Bakr said: Bakr ibn Abdurrahman narrated to us, Isa ibn Mukhtar narrated, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Children are the fruit of the heart; they cause cowardice, miserliness, and grief."
"3384","And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us with this."
"3385","Chapter: Dreams (95). Ishaq said: Abdah ibn Sulayman informed us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Harith at-Taymi, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Dreams are of three kinds: of them what a man tells himself and is nothing; of them what is from Satan, so when one sees what he dislikes let him seek refuge in Allah from the accursed Satan and spit to his left, for it will not harm him after that; and of them glad tidings from Allah. The dream of a Muslim is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood, so let him present it to one of sound advising judgment, let him speak good and interpret good. Awf ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) said: If it were a single pebble of the number of pebbles it would be much."
"3386","Yahya ibn Wadih al-Ansari informed us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When one of you sees a dream, let him present it to one of advising judgment, let him speak good and interpret good. I say: An-Nasa'i narrated it from the hadith of Ibn Ishaq, and it is not in al-Mujtaba; ash-Shaykhan and others brought it from the hadith of Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah, az-Zuhri, Abd Rabbihi ibn Sa'id, Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ja'far, Muhammad ibn Abdurrahman freedman of the family of Talhah, and Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, all of them from Abu Salamah with the basis of the hadith; in this wording is an addition not with them, nor with them the hadith of Awf ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"3387","And Ishaq said: Abu Amir al-Aqadi Abdulmalik ibn Amr informed us, Sulayman, that is Ibn Mughirah, narrated, from Humayd ibn Hilal, who said: Safiyyah said when she was among her family: I saw as if I and this one whom Allah sent, with an angel making us travel with his wing; they returned her dream upon her and said to her severe words."
"3388","Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn Musayyib, who said: A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said to Abu Bakr: I saw three moons falling in my room, or he said: in my lap. Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Good. Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari said: I heard people narrating that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was buried in the house of A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with them both), Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: This is one of your moons, and the best of them."
"3389","Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hisham, who said: I heard Muhammad say: Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) was the best interpreter of this ummah after the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3390","And al-Humaydi said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard Yahya ibn Sa'id narrating, from Sa'id ibn Musayyib, who said: A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I saw as if three moons fell in my room, so I asked Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him). He said: O A'ishah, if your dream is true, three of the best of the people of the earth will be buried in your house. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away and was buried, Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said to me: O A'ishah, this is the best of your moons, and one of them. Al-Hakim authenticated it from this route and also brought it from the hadith of Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) raised."
"3391","And al-Harith said: Dawud ibn Muhabbar narrated to us, Maysarah ibn Abd Rabbihi narrated, from Abu A'ishah as-Sa'di, from Yazid ibn Umar, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah and Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and mentioned a long hadith, and in it: Whoever claims a dream he did not see is like one who bore false witness, and will be burdened on the Day of Resurrection to tie between two barley grains, punished until he ties them, and he will not tie them."
"3392","And Abu Ya'la said: Amr ibn Muhammad an-Naqid narrated to us, Khidr ibn Muhammad al-Harrani narrated, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abu Zinad, from A'raj; Sulayman ibn Arib narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) say to Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dream of a Muslim is a part of forty parts of prophethood. Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: Of sixty. Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: He heard me say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and he says: Of sixty? Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: And I say: Al-Abbas ibn Abdulmuttalib (may Allah be pleased with him) said. Amr ibn Naqid said: I and our companions said: So it is with us, Allah willing: Al-Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3393","And al-Bazzar said: Ibrahim ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Ali ibn Hakim narrated, Amr ibn Hashim narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, and he mentioned it with the wording: The dream of a believer is glad tidings from Allah the Exalted, and a part of forty-six parts of prophethood. He said: I narrated it to Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both); he said: Al-Abbas ibn Abdulmuttalib said to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A part of fifty parts of prophethood."
"3394","And Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The dreams of prophets are true."
"3395","And Abu Ya'la said: Ibrahim ibn Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Tufayl, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And from Habib and Humayd, from Hasan (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While I was drawing water at night, black sheep came upon me, and dusty-white sheep; Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) came and drew a bucket or two buckets with weakness in them, and Allah forgive him. Then Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) came and it turned into a large bucket, filling the pools and watering those who came; I did not see a genius among people better in drawing than him. I interpreted the black sheep as the Arabs, and the dusty-white as the non-Arabs."
"3396","And al-Bazzar said: Muhammad ibn Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fadl narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Tufayl (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I saw in a sleeper's vision black sheep followed by dusty-white sheep; I interpreted the black as the Arabs and the dusty-white as the non-Arabs."
"3397","And al-Harith said: Sakan ibn Nafi' narrated to us, Imran ibn Hudayr narrated, from Abu Mijlaz, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I saw in a dream my head cut off, and I kept looking at it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed then said: With which eye did you look at your head when cut off? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not remain after that but a little until he passed away; they interpreted the cutting of his head as the death of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his looking as following his practices. End of the first part of the book al-Matalib al-Aliyah with the additions of the eight musnads, compiled by our shaykh the imam the scholar, shaykh of Islam, seal of memorizers, chief of judges Shihabuddin Abu Fadl Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Hajar al-Kinani al-Asqalani al-Misri ash-Shafi'i, may Allah cover him with His mercy, amen. On Saturday in the month of Rabi' al-Thani, one of the months of the year 875, in Mecca the honored; praise be to Allah, and may Allah bless our master Muhammad, his family and companions and grant peace. Allah suffices us and He is the best disposer."
"3398","In the name of Allah the Most Merciful the Most Compassionate. May Allah bless our master Muhammad, his family and companions and grant peace. My Lord, make easy, O Generous. Book of Faith and Tawhid (31). Chapter: Prohibition of the blood of one who testifies there is no god but Allah (1). Abu Bakr said: Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, Aban ibn Abdullah al-Bajali narrated, Ibrahim ibn Jarir narrated, from Jarir (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Yemen to fight them and call them; when they say: There is no god but Allah, their blood and wealth are forbidden to me."
"3399","Bakr ibn Abdurrahman narrated to us, Isa, that is Ibn Mukhtar, narrated, from Muhammad ibn Abdurrahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abu Zubayr, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever testifies there is no god but Allah and that I am Muhammad the Messenger of Allah, his blood is forbidden to me, except for three: one who leaves his religion, the married adulterer, and one who kills a soul unjustly."
"3400","And with it from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have a hypocrite neighbor who does such and such. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Does he say: There is no god but Allah? He said: Yes. He said: I was forbidden from killing those."
"3401","And al-Harith said: Dawud narrated to us, Maysarah narrated, from Abu A'ishah as-Sa'di, from Yazid ibn Umar, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah and Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and mentioned a long hadith, and in it: Behold, my Lord the Mighty and Majestic commanded me to fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah; when they say it they protect from me their blood and wealth except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah the Mighty and Majestic."
"3402","Chapter: Its virtue (2). Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated, from Mansur, from Shaqiq, who said: Abu Bakr met Talhah and said: Why do I see you gloomy this morning? He said: No, except a word I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: It obligates, but I did not ask him about it. He said: But I know it. He said: What is it? He said: There is no god but Allah. This chain is hasan if Shaqiq heard it from Talhah, and it is strange from the hadith of Abu Bakr."
"3403","Ishaq said: Jarir informed us, from Mansur, from Shaqiq, I was told, that Abu Bakr met Talhah, and he mentioned similar to it."
"3404","And Abu Ya'la said: Abbas ibn Walid narrated to us, Umar ibn Ali narrated, Abdurrahman ibn Ziyad ibn An'um narrated, he said: I heard Malik ibn Qays, who said: Uqbah ibn Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) came to Mu'awiyah while he was in Iliya, and soon left; he was sought but not found. He said: We came to him, and there he was praying in open land. He said: What brought you? We said: We came to renew our tie with you, or to fulfill your right. He (may Allah be pleased with him) said: With me is your reward: we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he mentioned a hadith, he said: Then Abu Bakr as-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Ibn Amir, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever testifies there is no god but Allah, his heart confirming his tongue, enters through whichever of the gates of Paradise he wishes."
"3405","And al-Harith said: Dawud ibn Muhabbar narrated to us, Maysarah ibn Abd Rabbihi narrated, from Abu A'ishah, from Yazid ibn Umar, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah and Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and mentioned the hadith, and in it: O people, whoever meets Allah the Exalted testifying there is no god but Allah sincerely enters Paradise. Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) stood and said: With my father and mother, O Messenger of Allah, how does one make it sincere? Does he not mix other than it with it? Clarify for us so we know. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Greed for the world, amassing it from unlawful, contentment with it, and people who speak the sayings of rabbis and do the deeds of the wicked; whoever meets Allah the Mighty and Majestic with none of these traits in him, saying: There is no god but Allah, enters Paradise."
"3406","And Ishaq said: Mu'ammal informed us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, Ziyad ibn Mikhraq narrated, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to me that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever dies believing in Allah and the Last Day, it is said to him: Enter Paradise through whichever of the eight gates of Paradise you wish. The hadith of Uqbah from Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) is in the Sahih with other than this wording. And the hadith of Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) preceded in the chapter of condemning pride in the Book of Manners."
"3407","And Ishaq said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, Isra'il narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Wahb al-Hamdani, who said: Mu'adh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) came to us in Yemen and said: I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to you, that you worship Allah the Exalted and associate nothing with Him, and that you obey me, I will not fail you in good; the return is to Allah the Exalted, and to Paradise and Hell, a stay without departure, and eternity without death. This chain is sahih."
"3408","And Abu Ya'la said: Amr ibn Dahhak narrated to us, my father narrated. And al-Bazzar said: And Bishr ibn Adam and Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us, both said: Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated, Mastur ibn Abbad Abu Hammam narrated, Thabit narrated, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I left no need nor hidden deed except I did it. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you not testify there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah? Three times. He said: Yes. He said: That covers that, the wording of Amr. Al-Bazzar said: We do not know Mastur narrated from Thabit except this."
"3409","And Ibn Abi Umar said: Marwan al-Fazari narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, who said: Marwan ibn Hakam said to Ayman ibn Khuraym: Will you not go out and fight with us? He said: My father and uncle were present at Badr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and enjoined upon me not to fight anyone who testifies there is no god but Allah; if you bring me acquittal from the Fire I will fight with you. He said: Go, we have no need of you."
"3410","And Abu Ya'la said: Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, Salih ibn Umar narrated, from Mutarrif, from Amir ash-Sha'bi, who said: When Marwan fought Dahhak ibn Qays he sent to Ayman ibn Khuraym al-Asadi and said: We love that you fight with us. He said: My father and uncle were present at Badr and enjoined upon me not to fight anyone who testifies there is no god but Allah; if you bring me acquittal I will fight with you. He said: Go, and he fell upon him and insulted him, so Ayman ibn Khuraym began to say poetry."
"3411","And Abu Ya'la said: Yahya ibn Abdulhamid narrated to us, Abdurrahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated, from his father, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is no loneliness upon the people of La ilaha illa Allah in their graves; as if I see the people of La ilaha illa Allah shaking dust from their heads saying: Praise be to Allah who removed grief from us."
"3412","Husayn ibn Aswad narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated, Umar ibn Hamzah narrated to me, Nafi' ibn Malik narrated to me, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: La ilaha illa Allah prevents the servant from the anger of Allah the Mighty and Majestic as long as they do not prefer care for their world over their religion; when they do that then say: La ilaha illa Allah the Mighty and Majestic, Allah the Mighty and Majestic says: You lie."
"3413","Amr ibn Husayn narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abdulmalik narrated, al-Awza'i narrated, from Abu Rafi', from Umm Hani (may Allah be pleased with her), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever says La ilaha illa Allah alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and praise and He is over all things capable, a hundred times, no sin follows him that day and no deed precedes him."
"3414","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uzayz narrated, Salamah ibn Rawh narrated, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab who said: Anas ibn Malik al-Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he descended a mountain pass, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walking alone; when the road opened before him he laughed and said takbir, so we said takbir for his takbir. Then he went a stone's throw, then laughed and said takbir, so we said takbir for his takbir. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went a stone's throw, then laughed and said takbir, so we said takbir for his takbir. Then we caught up with him (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); the people said: We said takbir for your takbir, but we do not know why you laughed? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gabriel (peace be upon him) came to me; when it opened he turned to me, Gabriel (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Rejoice and give glad tidings, that whoever says: La ilaha illa Allah alone without partner enters Paradise and is forbidden to the Fire."
"3415","And Musaddad said: Harith ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O so-and-so, did you do such and such? He said: No, by Him there is no god but Him, I did not do it, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) knew he had done it; he repeated upon him several times, each time he said: No, by Him there is no god but Him, I did not do it, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) knew he had done it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Your sin is expiated by your affirming La ilaha illa Allah."
"3416","And Abd said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Harith narrated with it."
"3417","And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Rabi' narrated to us, Harith narrated with it. And al-Bazzar brought it from this route and pointed to the sole narration of Harith ibn Ubayd with it. I say: Hammad ibn Maslamah opposed him; Ahmad brought it from his route and said: From Thabit, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both). Hammad said: Thabit did not hear it from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both); between them a man."
"3418","And Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Abu Nadr narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Abu Warqa, from Ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever says eleven times: La ilaha illa Allah alone without partner, One, Eternal, He did not beget nor was born, and there is none like Him, Allah the Blessed and Exalted writes for him two thousand thousand good deeds."
"3419","And Abd said: Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad narrated with it."
"3420","And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Nasr at-Tammar narrated to us, Hammad narrated with it. And a hadith on its virtue will come, Allah willing, in the chapter of seeking forgiveness."
"3421","Chapter: Islam is a condition for acceptance of deeds (3). Abu Bakr said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Shayban, from Mansur, from Mujahid, who said: Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Hisham ibn Mughirah used to feed food, honor the guest, join kinship, and free captives, meaning prisoners; had he lived he would have become Muslim, is there reward for him in that? She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your uncle used to give for the world, its mention and beauty, and never said one day: My Lord, forgive me my sin on the Day of Judgment."
"3422","And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Umm Salamah, who said: I said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned it."
"3423","And Abu Dawud said: Abbad ibn Rashid narrated to us, Hasan narrated, Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to us while we were in Medina, he said: Islam will come on the Day of Resurrection, and Allah the Mighty and Majestic says: You are Islam, and I am Peace; today by you I give, and by you I take."
"3424","And Musaddad said: Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, Khalid ibn Yazid as-Saksaki narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Muhammad ibn Abi Jahm, from Harith ibn Malik al-Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: He passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said to him: O Harith, how did you wake? He said: I woke a true believer. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Look at what you say, for everything has a reality, so what is your reality? He (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Have I not turned the world away from myself, thirsted my day, and kept my night awake, as if I look at the throne of my Lord manifest, as if I look at the people of Paradise visiting one another in it, and as if I look at the people of the Fire wailing in it, meaning crying out. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Harith, you knew, so hold fast, three times."
"3425","Chapter: Definition of Islam and faith (4). Musaddad said: Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub narrated, from Abu Qilabah, from a man of the people of Sham, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Submit and you will be safe. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what is Islam? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That you submit your heart to Allah the Blessed and Exalted, and Muslims are safe from your tongue and hand. He said: Which Islam is best? He said: Faith. He said: What is faith? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That you believe in Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers, and resurrection after death. He said: Which faith is best? He said: Migration. He said: What is migration? He said: That you abandon sin. He said: Which migration is best? He said: Struggle. He said: What is struggle? He said: That you fight the disbelievers when you see them, then do not betray or coward; then two deeds, they are among the best deeds, except like them an accepted pilgrimage or umrah."
"3426","And Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Isma'il narrated to us, and he mentioned it up to his saying: from your tongue and hand."
"3427","And al-Harith said: Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated, Sufyan ath-Thawri narrated, from Ayyub with it, up to his saying: then do not betray or coward."
"3428","And Abu Ya'la said: Ja'far ibn Mihran as-Sabbak narrated to us, Abdulwarith narrated, from Ayyub, in full, and added: and resurrection after death, and Paradise and Hell."
"3429","And Abu Bakr said: Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, Za'idah narrated, from Hisham, from Hasan, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), which Islam is best? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One from whose tongue and hand Muslims are safe. It was said: Which faith is best? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Patience and generosity. It was said: Which believers have most faith? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Best of them in character. It was said: Which struggle is best? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One whose horse is hamstrung and blood shed. It was said: Which prayer is best? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Long standing. It was said: Which charity is best? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Effort of one with little. It was said: Which migration is best? He said: That you abandon what Allah forbade you. They brought it abridged."
"3430","And Abu Ya'la said: Ubayd ibn Jannad al-Halabi narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Muhammad ibn Munkadir narrated, from his father, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about faith, he said: Patience and generosity."
"3431","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Zayd ibn Hubab narrated, from Ali ibn Mas'adah, from Qatadah, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Islam is open, and faith is in the heart. Then he points with his hand to his chest: Piety is here, piety is here."
"3432","And Musaddad said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ubayd ibn Umayr who said, I heard him say: Faith is fleeting."
"3433","Chapter: What the believer is given after his death (5). And Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Haytham narrated, from Thabit, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Exalted entrusts His believing servant with two angels writing his deeds; when Allah the Mighty and Majestic takes His believing servant, they say: O Lord, You entrusted us with Your believing servant writing his deeds, and You have taken him to You, so permit us to ascend to heaven. He, Majestic and Exalted, says: My heaven is filled with My angels prostrating to Me. They say: Permit us to dwell on earth. He the Mighty and Majestic says: My earth is filled with My creation prostrating to Me; but stand upon the grave of My servant, glorify Me, declare My oneness, magnify Me, praise Me until the Day of Resurrection, and write it for My servant."
"3434","Chapter: Love for Allah is of faith (6). At-Tayalisi said: Sa'q ibn Hazn narrated to us, from Aqil al-Ja'di, from Abu Ishaq, from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abdullah, do you know which bonds of Islam are firmest? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allegiance for Allah the Mighty and Majestic, love for Allah the Mighty and Majestic, and hatred for Allah the Blessed and Exalted."
"3435","And Abu Bakr said: Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, Sa'q ibn Hazn al-Bakri narrated with it."
"3436","And Abu Ya'la said: Shayban, that is Ibn Farrukh, narrated to us, Sa'q narrated with it."
"3437","Chapter: Rebuke against everyone who says La ilaha illa Allah (7). Abu Ya'la said: al-Qawariri narrated to us, Ibn Mahdi narrated, Abdulhamid ibn Bahram narrated to me, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated, Jundub ibn Sufyan a man of Bajilah narrated to me, he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a bearer of good news came from a detachment, informing him of Allah's victory by which He aided his detachment, and Allah's opening which He opened for them. He said: O Messenger of Allah, while we pursued the enemy, Allah the Exalted having routed them, I caught up with a man with the sword; when he sensed the sword striking him he turned while running and said: I am a Muslim, so I killed him, though he was only seeking refuge, O Prophet of Allah. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did you not split his heart and look, is he truthful or lying? He said: Had I split his heart it would not inform me; is his heart but a piece of flesh? He said: You killed him; neither what is in his heart you knew, nor his tongue you believed? He said: O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I will not seek forgiveness for you. He died, they buried him, and he became upon the surface of the earth three times. When his people saw that they were ashamed and feared what befell its carrying, so they cast him in a ravine of those ravines."
"3438","And he said: And Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Abdulhamid ibn Bahram narrated, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated, Jundub ibn Sufyan a man of Bajilah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated, he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned similar to it."
"3439","And al-Harith said: Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated, from al-Awza'i, from Harun ibn Ri'ab who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment, and it was opened for it; they sent their bearer of good news to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). While he informed him of Allah's opening for them, and the number Allah killed of them, he said: I singled out a man of them; when I overcame him to kill him he said: I am a Muslim, so I killed him. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You killed him though he said I am a Muslim? He said: O Messenger of Allah, he said that only seeking refuge. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why did you not split his heart? He said: How would I know that, O Messenger of Allah? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Neither his tongue you believed, nor his heart you knew; you are his killer, leave me, do not accompany me. He said: Then the man died, and the earth cast him out twice, so he was thrown in one of those valleys. Some of the people of knowledge said: The earth indeed covers one fouler than him, but it is a lesson."
"3440","Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abdurrahman ibn Abdullah, from Qatadah, from Abu Mijlaz, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you aims the spear at a man, if at the hollow of his throat he says: La ilaha illa Allah, let him raise the spear from him. He said: Abu Ubaydah said: Allah the Exalted made this word the safety of the Muslim and protection of his blood, and made jizyah the safety of the disbeliever and protection of his blood."
"3441","Chapter: Traits that admit to Paradise and protect blood (29). Ishaq said: And Abdurrazzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Zubayr ibn Awwam (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever guarantees me six, I guarantee him Paradise. It was said: What are they, O Messenger of Allah? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When he speaks he is truthful, when he promises he fulfills, when entrusted he is faithful; and one who lowers his gaze, guards his private part, and restrains his hand. I say: Thus Ishaq brought it in the musnad of Zubayr ibn Awwam (may Allah be pleased with him), and thus Ahmad ibn Mansur ar-Ramadi narrated it from Abdurrazzaq; others narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from Zubayr not attributed; if Ma'mar preserved it then it is sahih in chain, but disconnected; if Zuhayr preserved it then it is connected."
"3442","And Abu Bakr said: Mus'ab ibn Miqdam narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated, Abu Zumayl narrated, from Malik ibn Marthad az-Zimmani, from his father who said: Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What saves the servant from the Fire? He said: Faith in Allah. I said: O Prophet of Allah, is there deed with faith? He said: You give from what Allah provided you, or he gives from what Allah provided him. I said: O Prophet of Allah, what if he is poor, finding nothing to give? He said: He commands good and forbids evil. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what if he is tongueless, unable to command good or forbid evil? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let him make for one unskilled. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what if he is unskilled, not good at making? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He helps one overpowered. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what if he is weak unable to help one overpowered? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You do not want to leave your companion any good. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let him withhold his harm from people. I said: O Prophet of Allah, if he does this, will he enter Paradise? He said: No believer does a trait of these traits but it takes his hand until it admits him to Paradise."
"3443","And Abu Bakr said: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Mushir, from Ash'ath, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Jarud al-Abdi (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pledge to him, and said to him: That if I leave my religion and enter your religion, Allah the Exalted will not punish me in the Hereafter? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes."
"3444","And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us."
"3445","And Abu Bakr said: Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Uthman al-Batti, from Nu'aym ibn Abi Hind, from Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I was leaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to my chest, and he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says La ilaha illa Allah, sealed for him with it, enters Paradise."
"3446","And Abu Ya'la said: Sulayman ibn Abduljabbar narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated, from Bishr ibn Suhar, our elders narrated to us, that Iyadh narrated to them: The Messenger of Allah sent him in a detachment, and they brought answers of Bedouins; when he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), some of them claimed they were in Islam. He said: Who knows that? They said: Iyadh heard it from us. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Iyadh, did you hear it or witness it? I said: I heard the call to prayer: and La ilaha illa Allah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed them."
"3447","And Abu Ya'la said: Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Suwayd ibn Abdulaziz, from Thabit ibn Ajlan, from Sulaym ibn Amir who said: I heard Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go out and call among people: whoever testifies there is no god but Allah, Paradise is due for him. He (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I went out and Umar ibn Khattab met me and said: What is with you, O Abu Bakr? I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me, and mentioned it. He said: Return, for I fear they will rely upon it. I returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he said: What turned you back? I informed him of the saying of Umar (may Allah be pleased with him); he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He spoke truth."
"3448","And Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Hilal Abu Amr, Abu Burdah narrated, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: Whoever comes with testimony there is no god but Allah alone without partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, is forbidden to the Fire."
"3449","And Abu Ya'la said: Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Nuh ibn Qays narrated, Ash'ath al-Huddani narrated, from Makhul, from Amr ibn Abasah who said: An old man came leaning on a staff until he stood before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have treacheries and wicked deeds; will I be forgiven? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you not testify there is no god but Allah? He said: Yes, and I testify you are the Messenger of Allah. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your treacheries and wicked deeds are forgiven you."
"3450","Chapter (9). Ishaq said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim informed us, from Habib ibn Shahid, from Hasan (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The price of Paradise is La ilaha illa Allah. This is halted sahih."
"3451","Abdulmalik ibn Muhammad adh-Dhimari informed us, Ahmad ibn Sa'id ibn Rummanah informed me, my father informed me, he said: It was said to Wahb ibn Munabbih: Is not the key of Paradise La ilaha illa Allah? He said: Yes, but no key but has teeth; whoever comes to the door with its teeth, it is opened for him, and whoever does not come to the door with its teeth, it is not opened for him. This chain is hasan halted, and al-Bukhari suspended it from Wahb."
"3452","And Ishaq also said: Ata ibn Muslim al-Halabi informed us, from Ja'far ibn Burqan, from Wahb ibn Munabbih, who said: Faith is a leader, and deed a driver, and the soul stubborn between them; when the leader leads and the driver does not drive, that avails nothing; when the driver drives and the soul follows willingly or unwillingly."
"3453","And Musaddad said: Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Daylami, who said: From one of the three who used to serve Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him): That when he was dying, I said to him: Do I not see you have been attended? He said: Yes, and evil is this time for lying; whoever dies certain of three: knowing Allah the Exalted is true, the Hour is standing, and Allah raises those in graves, he said: He said a saying encouraging them in it, if it is not but he is forgiven, I do not know."
"3454","And Abd said: Ibrahim ibn Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ikrimah narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah the Blessed and Exalted said: Whoever of you knows I am able to forgive sins, I forgive him and I do not care, as long as he does not associate anything with Me."
"3455","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu Shihab narrated, from Layth, from Abu Fazarah, from Yazid ibn Asamm, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Three, whoever lacks them, Allah the Mighty and Majestic forgives him other than that for whom He wills: whoever dies not associating anything with Allah, not being a sorcerer following sorcerers, and not bearing hatred against his brother."
"3456","Chapter: Affirming faith for one who testifies the two testimonies and does righteous deeds (10). Ishaq said: Hammad ibn Amr al-Jazari informed us, from Zayd ibn Rufay', from Ma'bad al-Juhani, who said: There was a man called Yazid ibn Umayrah as-Saksaki, a student of Mu'adh ibn Jabal; he mentioned the hadith, he said: Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him) died and Yazid joined Kufa; he came to the gathering of Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) and he was not there; they began mentioning faith. Some said: Had I witnessed I am a believer I would witness I am in Paradise. Yazid said: I witness I am a believer, but I do not witness I am in Paradise. Then Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) came and was informed of that. Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) said to Yazid: Is it so? He said: Yes. He said: From where is that? Yazid said: O Abu Abdurrahman, Allah the Exalted says: Those who believed, those who were Jews, Sabeans, Christians, Magians, and those who associated. Of which of these are you, O Abu Abdurrahman? He said: Of those who believed. He said: Yes truly. Then he said to Yazid: By Allah, were you a student of Mu'adh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him)? He said: Yes. Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Mu'adh was a nation devout, upright, and not of the polytheists. His companions said: Abraham was a nation devout to Allah. Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him) was a nation devout to Allah, upright."
"3457","And Abu Bakr said: Ali ibn Hashim narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Minhal ibn Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Upon my mother is a believing neck, and with me is a black non-Arab neck. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring her. He brought her. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you testify there is no god but Allah? She said: Yes. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you testify I am the Messenger of Allah? She said: Yes. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Free her."
"3458","And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Harith Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah al-Fazari narrated, from Muhammad ibn Abi Qays, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Mujahid ibn Jabr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) who said: Abu Razin al-Uqayli (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to me, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: I and you will surely drink of milk whose color has not changed. I said: How does Allah give life to the dead? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did you not pass by barren land, then pass by it fertile, then pass by it barren, then pass by it fertile? I said: Yes. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Likewise resurrection. He said: I said: How do I know I am a believer? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one of this ummah, or of my ummah, does a good deed, knowing it is good and Allah the Mighty and Majestic will reward him with good for it, or does an evil deed, and that Allah the Exalted will reward him with evil for it or forgive it, except he is a believer."
"3459","Chapter: Faith remains when its possessor is compelled to disbelief (11). Ishaq said: Abdurrazzaq informed us, Ma'mar narrated, from Abdulkarim al-Jazari, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Muhammad ibn Ammar ibn Yasir, who said: The polytheists took Ammar ibn Yasir (may Allah be pleased with him) and tortured him; he yielded to them in some of what they wanted from him. He complained that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How do you find your heart? He said: At rest with faith. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If they return, return. And it will come, Allah willing, from another route, with another wording, in the commentary of Surah Nahl."
"3460","Chapter: Traits of faith (12). Abu Ya'la said: Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Masmuli narrated, from Qasim ibn Mukhawwal al-Bahzi, from his father, who said: I said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Advise me. He said: Establish prayer, give zakat, fast Ramadan, perform hajj and umrah, command good and forbid evil... the hadith."
"3461","And Abd ibn Humayd said: Umar ibn Sa'id ad-Dimashqi narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abdulaziz at-Tanukhi narrated, from Makhul, from Umm Ayman (may Allah be pleased with her) who said: She heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advising some of his family, and he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not associate anything with Allah even if cut or burned with fire, and beware disobedience for it angers Allah the Mighty and Majestic... the hadith."
"3462","And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Bakr ibn Zanjawayh narrated to us, Abu Mushir narrated, Sa'id ibn Abdulaziz narrated with it."
"3463","And Abd said: Umar ibn Sa'id narrated to us, other than Sa'id narrated, from az-Zuhri: The one advised with this advice is Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"3464","And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Yasir Ammar narrated to us, Abu Miqdam Hisham ibn Ziyad narrated, my father narrated to me, from Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn Salam, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Modesty is of faith."
"3465","And Musaddad said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: Patience is half of faith, gratitude two-thirds of faith, certainty is all faith."
"3466","And al-Humaydi said: Sufyan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated, from Ma'bad ibn Ka'b, from his uncle or from his mother, raised: O people, shabbiness is of faith."
"3467","And Abd said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Bishr ibn Numayr informed us, from Qasim, from Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him), from Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) that he used to say: From the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he used to say: The bonds of faith are four: and Islam followers; the bonds of faith: that you believe in Allah alone, and in Muhammad, and what he brought, and believe in Allah, and know you will be raised after death; and establishing prayer, giving zakat, fasting Ramadan, hajj of the House, and struggle in Allah's path the Exalted. Bishr is very weak."
"3468","And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Yusuf al-Jizi narrated to us, Mu'ammal narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, Amr ibn Malik an-Nukri narrated, from Abu Jawza, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), Hammad said: I do not know but he raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The bonds of Islam and pillars of religion are three, upon them Islam is founded; whoever leaves one of them is a disbeliever whose blood is lawful: testimony there is no god but Allah, establishing the prescribed prayer, and fasting Ramadan. Then Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: You find him with much wealth, not paying zakat, yet thereby a disbeliever, but his blood is not lawful; you find him with much wealth, not having performed hajj, yet thereby a disbeliever, but his blood is not lawful."
"3469","And Abd and Harith both said: Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Abdurrahman ibn Ziyad narrated, from Abdullah ibn Rashid freedman of Uthman ibn Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Before the Merciful the Blessed and Exalted is a tablet with three hundred and fifteen laws; the Merciful says: By My might and majesty, no servant of My servants comes to Me not associating anything with Me, with one of them in him, but enters Paradise."
"3470","And Abu Ya'la said: Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ad-Dawraqi narrated to us, Abu Abdurrahman al-Muqri narrated with it."
"3471","And al-Harith said: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Abu Ja'far narrated, Rabi' ibn Anas informed us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever leaves the world upon sincerity to Allah and His worship without partner, establishing prayer and giving zakat, leaves it while Allah the Mighty and Majestic is pleased with him. Anas said: That is Allah's religion which the messengers brought and conveyed from their Lord before the commotion of narrations and differing of desires. Allah the Mighty and Majestic says: If they repent, he said: They cast off idols and their worship, and establish prayer and give zakat, then leave their way free."
"3472","Chapter: Religion is ease (13). Ishaq said: Abu Amir al-Aqadi informed us, Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Adra', who said: I was guarding one night the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I stood, he took my hand and leaned upon it; we came upon a man praying in the mosque raising his voice. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perhaps he is showing off. I said: O Messenger of Allah, he prays and supplicates. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) let go my hand and said: You will not attain this matter by struggling, or he said by harshness. He said: Then we went out another night and passed a man praying raising his voice. I said: O Messenger of Allah, perhaps he is showing off. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, but he is tender-hearted. He said: Then the man was Abdullah Dhu Bijadayn (may Allah be pleased with him), and the other a Bedouin. This chain is hasan."
"3473","And Abu Ya'la said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated, from Dawud ibn Qays, from Zayd ibn Aslam (may Allah be pleased with him) similar to it."
"3474","And Musaddad said: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Yunus narrated, from Ziyad ibn Mikhraq, from a man of Aslam, who said: Among us were three who accompanied the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Buraydah, Mihjan, and Sukbah. Mihjan said to Buraydah: Will you not pray as Sukbah prays? He said: No, you saw me coming with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Uhud walking, his hand in my hand; he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man praying and said: Do you see him serious, do you see him truthful? I went to praise him. When we drew near he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pulled his hand from my hand and said: Woe to you, be silent, do not let him hear lest you destroy him; the best of your religion is its easiest."
"3475","And Musaddad also said: Khalid narrated to us, Husayn ibn Qays narrated. And Abu Ya'la said: Wahb, that is Ibn Baqiyyah, narrated to us, Khalid narrated, from Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed people and said: Allah the Mighty and Majestic gave every rightful one his right; Allah ordained obligations, legislated practices, set limits, permitted lawful and forbade unlawful, legislated Islam and made it easy, spacious, wide, and did not make it narrow. O people, there is no faith for one with no trust, no religion for one with no covenant. Whoever breaks Allah's protection, He seeks him; whoever breaks my protection, I dispute him; whoever I dispute, I overcome him with proof; whoever breaks my protection, my intercession does not reach him, nor does he come to my Pool. Behold, Allah the Mighty and Majestic permitted killing only in three: an apostate after faith, an adulterer after chastity, or killer of a soul, killed for it. O Allah, have I conveyed."
"3476","Chapter: Prescribed punishments are expiations (14). Musaddad said: Abdulwahid narrated to us. Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Abu Nasr narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, both, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather (may Allah be pleased with them), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: I pledge you upon not associating anything with Allah, not stealing, not committing adultery, not killing the soul Allah forbade except by right; whoever of you commits this, its punishment hastened for him, it is expiation; whoever is veiled, his matter is to Allah, if He wills He punishes him, if He wills He has mercy on him; whoever commits nothing of it, I guarantee him Paradise. The wording of Abdulwahid; in Hammad's narration: Do you know upon what you pledged me? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon not associating anything with Allah, and the rest similar; he said: It is expiation of his sin; he said: His reckoning is upon Allah the Mighty and Majestic."
"3477","Chapter: Example of the believer (15). Abu Ya'la said: Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Saminah narrated to us, Abdurrahman al-Muharibi narrated, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) who said: The example of the believer is like the palm tree; if you consult him he benefits you, if you walk with him he benefits you, if you share with him he benefits you."
"3478","Suwayd, that is Ibn Sa'id, narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated, from Layth, similar to it."
"3479","And Abu Bakr said: Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Ibn Mubarak, from Mus'ab ibn Thabit, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The example of the believer among the people of faith is like the head to the body; the believer pains for the people of faith as the body pains for what is in the head."
"3480","Chapter: Signs of faith (16). Al-Harith said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Layth ibn Sa'd narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu Khayr, that he heard Ibn Abi Rafi' say: A man narrated to him that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, when he asked him: What is faith, O Messenger of Allah? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Faith is that you believe in Allah the Exalted and His Messenger. Then he asked him a second time, and he said similar to that. Then he asked him a third time, and said: Would you love that I tell you what is pure faith? He said: That I wanted. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pure faith is when you do evil or wrong someone: your male or female slave, or one of the Muslims, you give charity and fast; and when you do good you rejoice."
"3481","Abu Ya'la said: Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Ali ibn Hashim ibn al-Barid narrated to us, he said: I heard al-A'mash narrating from Abu Ishaq, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every character the believer is molded upon or folded upon, except treachery and lying. Ali ibn Hashim doubted."
"3482","Al-Bazzar said: Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Sa'igh narrated to us, Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, with this, and he said: We do not know anyone who raised it as marfu' except Ali ibn Hashim."
"3483","Muhammad ibn Jami' narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Dawud, from Raja' ibn Haywah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A servant does not reach pure faith until he abandons joking and lying, and abandons argument even if he is right."
"3484","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Silah ibn Zufar narrating from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Islam is eight shares: Islam is a share, prayer is a share, zakah is a share, hajj is a share, fasting Ramadan is a share, enjoining good is a share, forbidding evil is a share, and jihad in the path of Allah Almighty is a share, and he has failed who has no share."
"3485","Al-Bazzar said: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, with this, as mawquf."
"3486","Al-Bazzar said: And Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Yazid ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yazid ibn Ata' narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Silah, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), as marfu'. Al-Bazzar said: None raised it as musnad except Yazid, and al-Daraqutni and others said: The correct view is that it is mawquf."
"3487","Abu Ya'la said: Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Hubayb ibn Habib, brother of Hamzah al-Zayyat, narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Islam is eight shares, and he mentioned it. I say: Habib erred in it, and the correct view is from Abu Ishaq, from Silah, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, as his statement, as has passed."
"3488","Chapter: The virtue of one who believes in the unseen. Ishaq said: Abu Amir al-Aqadi Abd al-Malik ibn Amr informed us, Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: Do you know which people of faith have the most excellent faith? They said: O Messenger of Allah, the angels. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are so, and that is rightfully theirs, and what prevents them, when Allah Almighty has given them the station He gave them; rather, others. We said: O Messenger of Allah, the prophets. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are so, and that is rightfully theirs; rather, others. We said: O Messenger of Allah, who are they? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People who come after me, in the loins of men, who believe in me though they never saw me, and find hanging sheets and act upon what is in them; these are the best of the people of faith in faith. Muhammad is weak in hadith, poor in memory."
"3489","Abu Ya'la said: Mus'ab ibn Abd Allah al-Zubayri narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: Inform me of the best of the people of faith in faith? They said: O Messenger of Allah, the angels. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are so, and that is rightfully theirs, and what prevents them, when Allah Almighty has given them the station He gave them; rather, others. They said: The prophets whom Allah Almighty honored with His message and prophethood. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are so, and that is rightfully theirs, and what prevents them, when Allah Almighty has given them the station He gave them. They said: O Messenger of Allah, the martyrs who were martyred with the prophets. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are so, and that is rightfully theirs, and what prevents them, when Allah Almighty honored them with martyrdom with the prophets; rather, others. They said: Who, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Peoples in the loins of men, and he mentioned the hadith."
"3490","Abu Musa Muhammad narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adiyy narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, with it."
"3491","Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Yahya ibn Abi Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Umarah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, he said: I was sitting with Abd Allah, may Allah be pleased with him, and they mentioned the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the precedence of virtue they had. He said: The affair of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was clear to whoever saw him. By the One besides whom there is no god, there is none better than faith in the unseen. Then he recited: Alif Lam Mim, That is the Book in which there is no doubt, a guidance for the God-fearing, up to: the successful."
"3492","Chapter: The multitude of the people of Islam. Abu Bakr said: al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Jabir al-Dabbi narrated to us, from Mujammi' ibn Attab ibn Shumayr, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have an old aged father and brothers, so shall I go to them that perhaps they will accept Islam, and bring them to you? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If they accept Islam, it is better for them, and if they refuse, Islam is wide and spacious."
"3493","Chapter: Explanation of the major sins. Abu Bakr said: Malik ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Ja'far narrated to us, from Abu Harun, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer when he commits it, nor does the thief steal while he is a believer when he steals, nor does one plunder a plunder of honor to which people raise their heads while he is a believer."
"3494","Isma'il ibn Abd al-Karim narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Aqil narrated to us, from his father, from Wahb, he said: I asked Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him: Did you hear the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer when he commits it, nor does he steal when he steals while he is a believer? He said: I did not hear it, and I was informed that Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, used to say it."
"3495","Al-Harith said: Umar ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see the adulterer and the drinker of wine, what do you say about them? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: They are obscenities, and in them is punishment. Shall I not inform you of the greatest of major sins? We said: Yes. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Associating partners with Allah; Allah Almighty said: And whoever associates partners with Allah has fabricated a great sin. And disobedience to parents. Then He Almighty said: Be grateful to Me and to your parents; to Me is the return. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was reclining, then sat up and said: And indeed false speech, and indeed false speech."
"3496","Abd al-Aziz ibn Aban narrated to us, al-Sari ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Qays ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Disbelief in Allah is for one to claim a lineage that is not known, and disbelief in Allah is to disown a lineage even if slight."
"3497","Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Bishr narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Five shall not enter Paradise: the habitual drinker of wine, the severer of kinship, the believer in magic, the reminder of favors, and the soothsayer."
"3498","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Layth, from Uthman, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever deceives a man regarding his family or his servant is not of us."
"3499","Abu Ya'la said: Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Atiq and Hisham, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, he said: Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, was asked about the major sins. He said: Everything Allah forbade in the Qur'an is a major sin, and he mentioned the glance."
"3500","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salman narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Ayyub, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no servant who worships Allah Almighty associating nothing with Him, establishes prayer, gives zakah, fasts Ramadan, and avoids the major sins, except that he will enter Paradise. It was said: What are the major sins? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Associating partners with Allah Almighty, and killing a soul. Sahih."
"3501","Musaddad said: Khalid narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Qays, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever walks to the authority of Allah on earth to humiliate it, Allah Almighty will humiliate his neck on the Day of Resurrection along with what is stored for him of punishment; and the authority of Allah Almighty is the Book of Allah Almighty and the Sunnah of His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3502","Chapter: The explanation that the origin of things is permissibility. Musaddad said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us."
"3503","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah said: Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, both said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Makhul, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty imposed obligations so do not neglect them, set limits so do not transgress them, prohibited things so do not violate them, and remained silent about things without forgetfulness as a mercy for you, so do not ask about them. Its men are trustworthy, except that it is disconnected."
"3504","Abu Ya'la said: al-Qawariri narrated to us, Muslim ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata' ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you enter upon your Muslim brother, eat from his food and do not ask, and drink from his drink and do not ask."
"3505","Chapter: The foundations of religion. Ishaq said: Kathir ibn Hisham informed us, Furat ibn Salman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ulwan narrated to us, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Three are from the foundation of religion: gathering behind every righteous and wicked one, praying over whoever dies of the people of the qiblah, and striving under the rule of whoever it be; your reward is yours."
"3506","Abu Bakr said: Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Sinan narrated to us, from Abu al-Mubarak, from Ata', from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever deems lawful what is forbidden in it has not believed in the Qur'an."
"3507","Abd ibn Humayd narrated it from Abu Bakr. Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Sinan differed from his father and said: Ata', from Mujahid, from Suhayb. Ibn Adiyy mentioned it."
"3508","Abu Bakr said: Sa'id ibn Shurahbil narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj, from Busr ibn Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A man said to his brother: Allah will not forgive you; so it was said to him: Rather you, Allah will not forgive. Sahih."
"3509","Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abd Allah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A man stepped on the neck of a man while he was prostrating, and he said: You stepped on my neck while I am prostrating? By Allah, Allah will not forgive you. He said: He swore upon Allah Almighty, so He forgave him."
"3510","Chapter: The religion is the religion of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ibn Abi Umar said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: Mu'awiyah said to Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both: Are you upon the religion of Ibn Abi Talib? He said: No, nor the religion of Ibn Affan. Mu'awiyah said: Then upon which religion are you? He said: Upon the religion of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3511","Chapter: The explanation that deeds are part of faith. Ishaq said: Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Muqri' and al-Mula'i informed us, both said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from al-Qasim, he said: A man came to Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, and asked him about faith, so he recited: Righteousness is not that you turn your faces toward the east and the west, but righteousness is whoever believes in Allah, up to His Almighty saying: Those are the truthful and those are the God-fearing. The man said: I did not ask you about righteousness. Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about what you asked me, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited to him as I recited to you, and he said to him what you said to me; when he refused to be satisfied, he said to him: Come near, so he came near. He said: The believer, when he does a good deed it pleases him and he hopes for its reward, and when he does an evil deed it grieves him and he fears its punishment. This is disconnected, and it has a sounder path in the tafsir."
"3512","Chapter: Taking lesson from the ending. al-Harith said: Ahmad ibn Ishaq informed us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, Yunus and Humayd among others, from al-Hasan, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No blame on you not to hasten regarding anyone among you until you see how his work is sealed. Al-Hasan, may Allah be pleased with him, used to say: O Allah, make the best of our deeds their endings, and make their reward Paradise. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, make the best of our deeds what is nearest our appointed terms, and make the best of our days the day of meeting You."
"3513","Chapter: Divine decree. Its hadiths preceded in the warning against innovations. Abu Ya'la said: Zuhayr narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Yunus narrating from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hunaydah, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah wants to create a soul, the angel of the wombs says turning aside: O Lord, male or female? So Allah Almighty decrees His command; then he says: O Lord, wretched or happy? So Allah Almighty decrees His command; then he writes between his eyes what he will meet, even the stumble he stumbles."
"3514","Al-Bazzar said: Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the sperm-drop is created in the womb, the angel of the wombs says: O Lord, what do I write? So Allah Almighty decrees His command, and he says: Male or female? So Allah Almighty decrees His command, the hadith. Al-Bazzar said: Salih alone narrated it from al-Zuhri, meaning from Salim."
"3515","Al-Harith said: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Uthman al-Basri narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Mulaykah, from his father, from A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever speaks about the decree in anything will be asked about it on the Day of Resurrection."
"3516","Hawdhah narrated to us, Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, from a man, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The beginning of the destruction of nations was from the side of the decree, and you will be tested, O community, by them; if you meet them or encounter them, ask them, or be you the askers, and do not enable them to ask."
"3517","Abu Ya'la said: Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Sawwar ibn Mus'ab al-Kufi narrated to us, from Kulayb ibn Wa'il, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever denies the decree or disputes in it has rejected what I brought and disbelieved in what was revealed to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3518","Ammar narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, Qatadah, Abd Allah al-Danaj and Matar al-Warraq narrated to us, all from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) exited from the door of the house intending the chamber, and heard people disputing among themselves about the decree, saying: Did not Allah Almighty say such and such verse? Did not Allah Almighty say such and such verse? He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) opened the door of the chamber as if pomegranate seeds had burst on his face, and said: Were you commanded this? Or were you sent for this? Those before you perished only by the likes of this; they struck the Book of Allah Almighty part with part. Allah commanded you a command so follow it, and forbade you so refrain. He said: The people after that were not heard speaking about it, meaning therein, until Ma'bad al-Juhani came, and al-Hajjaj seized him and killed him."
"3519","Al-Harith said: al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Hamzah al-Nasibi narrated to us, from Ata' ibn Abi Rabah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) exited to his Companions while they were discussing the decree, so he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were you commanded this? You have taken to two valleys whose end you will never reach; by them the generations before you perished. Beware, beware."
"3520","Abu Ya'la said: Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Sinan narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty seized a handful and said: For Paradise by My mercy; and seized a handful and said: For the Fire, and I do not care."
"3521","Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Sinan al-Abdi narrated to us, with it."
"3522","Al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Shihab ibn Khirash narrated to us, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I fear for my community after me five: denial of the decree, and belief in the stars."
"3523","Al-Harith said: Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb narrated to us, Harun Abu al-Ala' narrated to us, from Rabi'ah, as marfu': The destruction of my community is in three: the Qadariyyah, tribal partisanship, and narration without verification."
"3524","Abu Ya'la said: Ahmad ibn Jamil narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Rabah ibn Zayd, from Umar ibn Habib, from al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazzah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that he narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first thing Allah Almighty created is the Pen, and He commanded it to write everything."
"3525","Wasil ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Layth, from Sa'id ibn Amir, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: This tribe of Quraysh remains safe until you turn them back from their religion as shielding disbelievers. A man stood to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, am I in Paradise or in the Fire? He said: In Paradise. Then another stood to him and said: Am I in Paradise or in the Fire? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In the Fire. Then he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep silent toward me as long as I keep silent toward you; were it not that you would not bury one another, I would inform you of your fill from the people of the Fire until you would know them at death; and if I were commanded to do it I would do it. Layth is weak."
"3526","Al-Harith said: Yahya ibn Abbad narrated to us, Bahr narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There was never an origin of heresy except that its beginning was denial of the decree."
"3527","Affan narrated to us, Hassan narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Masruq narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn Abi Burdah, from his father, he said: I came to A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, and she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Birds run by decree, and the good omen used to please him (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3528","Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, Abu Qahdham narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the decree is mentioned, withhold; and when my Companions are mentioned, withhold."
"3529","Dawud narrated to us, Salih al-Murri narrated to us, from al-Hasan, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it, and he added: And when the stars are mentioned, withhold."
"3530","Al-Harith also said: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, Bakr ibn Abd Allah, son of the sister of Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad, narrated to us, from Atiyyah ibn Atiyyah, from Ibrahim ibn Isma'il, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, he said: I was sitting with Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib when one of the people said: O Abu Muhammad, men say: Allah Almighty decreed everything except evil. He said: By Allah, I never saw Sa'id angry with anger like his anger that day, until he was about to stand; then he said: They did it? Woe to them, if you knew; by Allah, I heard a hadith about them sufficient as evil for them. He said: I said: What is it, may Allah have mercy on you, O Abu Muhammad? He said: He looked at me, his anger having subsided, and said: Rafi' ibn Khadij, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to me, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will be in my community peoples who disbelieve in Allah and in the decree though they do not perceive, as the Jews and Christians disbelieved. He said: I said: May I be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah, how do they say? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They say: Good is from Allah, and evil is from Iblis. He said: Yet they recite the Book of Allah Almighty upon that, and disbelieve in Allah Almighty after faith and knowledge. What my community will meet from them of enmity, hatred and disputation! Those are the heretics of this community; in their time will be the injustice of the ruler, what injustice, deviation and favoritism. Then Allah Almighty will send upon them a plague, so most of them perish; then will be transformation and swallowing, and few among them will be saved. All that day have little joy and severe grief. Then will be transformation; Allah Almighty will transform most of those into apes and pigs. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wept until we wept for his weeping. It was said: What is this weeping, O Messenger of Allah? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Out of mercy for the wretched; for among them are the strenuous and the worshipful, though they are not the first to precede to this saying, and it constrained him. Most of those who perished of the Children of Israel perished by it. It was said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), what is faith in the decree? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That you believe in Allah alone, know that none besides Him owns harm or benefit, believe in Paradise and the Fire, and know that Allah Almighty created them before creation, then created His creation, and made whom He willed of them for Paradise and whom He willed of them for the Fire."
"3531","Abu Ya'la said: Ahmad al-Dawraqi narrated to us, al-Muqri' narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Amr ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, and he mentioned it at length."
"3532","Ishaq said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas: That he heard a man say: Evil is not by decree. Ibn Abbas said: Between us and the people of the decree is: Those who associate partners will say: If Allah had willed we would not have associated partners, we nor our fathers, until he reached: Had He willed He would have guided you all. Ibn Abbas said: And incapacity and shrewdness are from the decree. Tawus said: The two disputants of the Qadariyyah speak without knowledge, so avoid speech about the decree. He said: Iblis met Isa son of Maryam and said: Do you not know that nothing befalls you except what is decreed for you, so go to the peak of the mountain and throw yourself from it, and see whether you live or not? Isa said: Allah says: The servant ought not to test Me, and whatever I will I do. Ma'mar said: al-Zuhri said: Iblis met Isa son of Maryam, and he mentioned the like, and said: Isa said to him: The servant does not test his Lord, but Allah tests His servant, so he silenced him."
"3533","He said: I am Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid, al-Awza'i narrated to me, from al-Ala' ibn Uyaynah, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Makki, from Ibn Abbas: That a man came to Makkah speaking about the decree, so he said: Show him to me that I may seize his head; by Allah, if his neck falls into my hand I will crush it, and if his nose falls into my hand I will bite it. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): As if I see the women of Banu Fahm circumambulating al-Khazraj, their buttocks shaking, as polytheists; and this is the first polytheism in Islam. By Allah, their evil will not end until they remove Allah from decreeing good, as they removed Him from decreeing evil. Baqiyyah said: So I met al-Ala' ibn Uyaynah and he narrated it to me, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd, from Mujahid ibn Jabr Abu al-Hajjaj, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3534","Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Salim al-Khurasani narrated to us, from Nafi', from al-Qasim, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among what Allah Almighty sent down in the Books: I am Allah, there is no god but Me; I decreed good and evil."
"3535","Ishaq said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid informed us, al-Zubaydi Muhammad ibn al-Walid narrated to me, from Rashid ibn Sa'd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, from Hisham ibn Hakim ibn Hizam, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, are deeds begun anew or has the decree been decided? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah Almighty brought forth the progeny of Adam, peace be upon him, from his back and made them witness over themselves, then poured them from His two hands, He said: These for Paradise and these for the Fire; the people of Paradise are facilitated to the deeds of the people of Paradise, and the people of the Fire are facilitated to the deeds of the people of the Fire. This is a strange hadith."
"3536","Abu Ya'la said: Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Attiyyah, from Mansur, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, as marfu': The Magians of this community, even if they fast and pray, meaning the Qadariyyah."
"3537","Abd said: Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Bilal, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion. Its men are trustworthy except Ibn Abi Layla did not hear from Bilal, may Allah be pleased with him."
"3538","Abu Ya'la said: Isma'il ibn Khalid al-Qurashi narrated to us, Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Abu al-Wasil Abd al-Hamid ibn Wasil, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say in his supplication: O Guardian of Islam and its people, keep me firm in it until I meet You with it."
"3539","Abu Bakr said: Abd Allah ibn Bakr al-Sahmi narrated to us, Bishr ibn Numayr narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah Almighty created creation, decreed the decree, took the covenant of the prophets, while His Throne was upon the water, He took the people of the right by His right hand and the people of the left by His other hand, and both hands of the Most Merciful are right; then He said: O companions of the right, and they said: At Your service, our Lord, and blessed; He said: Am I not your Lord? They said: Yes. Then He said: O companions of the left, and they said: At Your service, our Lord, and blessed; He said: Am I not your Lord? They said: Yes. Then He mixed some of them with others. He said: One among them said: Our Lord, why did You mix us? He said: And they have works besides that which they shall do, up to His saying: We were heedless of this. Then He returned them to the loins of Adam, peace be upon him. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty created creation, decreed the decree, took the covenant of the prophets while His Throne was upon the water; the people of Paradise are its people and the people of the Fire are its people. He said: One said: O Prophet of Allah, what about deeds? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Each people work according to their station. Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: We strive hard. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about deeds, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, consider deeds: is it something begun anew or finished? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rather it is finished."
"3540","Al-Tayalisi said: Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr al-Hanafi narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and he mentioned from its beginning up to His saying: While His Throne was upon the water; the people of Paradise are its people and the people of the Fire are its people."
"3541","Musaddad said: Hammad narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Salih, as a narration: Allah Almighty created the heavens and the earth, created Paradise and the Fire, created Adam, then scattered his progeny in His two hands, then poured them out and said: These for this, and I do not care, and these for this, and I do not care. He wrote the people of Paradise and what they will do, and wrote the people of the Fire and what they will do, then folded the book and it was lifted. Mursal."
"3542","Ibn Abi Umar said: Abd al-Rahim ibn Zayd narrated to us, from his father, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, as marfu': Sufficiency for a man as happiness is that he be guided in his religion."
"3543","Musaddad said: Mu'tamir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A servant does not believe so his faith is complete until he believes in the decree, its good and its evil, its bitter and its sweet, its harm and its benefit. This is mursal, and Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd is weak."
"3544","Abu Bakr said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Harun, from Abu Sa'id, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Adam and Musa, peace be upon them both, disputed; Musa said to Adam: You whom Allah created with His hand, breathed into you of His spirit, settled you in His Paradise, yet you ruined us, led us astray, and mentioned what Allah willed of this. Adam, peace be upon him, said to him: You whom Allah chose with His words and His messages, yet you blame me for a matter Allah decreed upon me before He created the heavens and the earth? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So Adam overcame Musa, so Adam overcame Musa."
"3545","Abd ibn Humayd said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Abu Harun, and he mentioned it as marfu', except that he said: Do you blame me for a matter decreed upon me before I was created? So Adam overcame Musa, so Adam overcame Musa."
"3546","Al-Harith said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abu Harun, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Adam met Musa, peace be upon them both, and Musa said: O Adam, and he mentioned it, and added therein: And He made His angels prostrate to you, and he did not say: So you ruined us and led us astray. He said: You did what you did and expelled your progeny from Paradise, and added: And He brought you near as a confidant and gave you the Torah. In how many years do you find the sin I committed written upon me before I did it? He said: Forty years. The rest is similar."
"3547","Abu Ya'la said: al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard Ashras narrating from Sayf, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Salih ibn Sarj, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not believe in the decree, its good and its evil, I am free of him. This is a weak chain."
"3548","Chapter: Children. Musaddad said: Hammad narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sadaqah, he said: I said to Muhammad ibn Sirin, this hadith: Every newborn is born upon the fitrah, who said it? He said: He said it who knew it."
"3549","Abu Ya'la said: Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Abu Hamzah al-Attar Ishaq ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from al-Aswad ibn Sari', may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every child is born upon the fitrah until his tongue expresses for him; then his parents make him a Jew and make him a Christian."
"3550","Chapter: The splitting of the community. al-Harith said: Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abu Ja'far narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib, he said: I was in Damascus when seventy heads of the Haruriyyah were brought and set up. Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, came, entered the mosque, prayed two rak'ahs, then exited and stood over them, shedding tears for a while. Then he said: What does Iblis do with the people of Islam? Three times. Then he said: O Abu Ghalib, you are in a land of many desires and many terrors. I said: Yes. He said: May Allah protect you from them. I said: Why do you shed your tears? He said: Out of mercy for them; they were of the people of Islam. Then he said: Do you recite Surah Al Imran? I said: Yes. He said: Recite this verse: He it is who sent down upon you the Book, in it are decisive verses. He said: These had deviation in their hearts, so they were led astray. Then he recited: On the day faces whiten. I said: Are they these? He said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Children of Israel split into seventy-one sects, all in the Fire except the great multitude. A man beside me said: O Abu Umamah, do you not see what the great multitude does? He said: Upon them what they bear and upon you what you bear; And if you obey him you will be guided. Hearing and obedience are better than disobedience and division; they judge for us then kill us. He said: I said to him: This hadith, did you narrate something or hear it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or do you say it from your opinion? He said: Then I would be audacious to narrate to you without hearing it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I heard it from him twice or thrice, until they said seven times."
"3551","Dawud ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Shihab Abd Rabbih ibn Nafi' narrated to us, from Amr ibn Qays al-Mula'i, from Dawud ibn al-Sulayk, from Abu Ghalib, he said: I was in Basrah in the time of Abd al-Malik when the heads of the Khawarij were brought, and he mentioned the like. Al-Tirmidhi, Ibn Majah and Ahmad narrated it in brief."
"3552","Abu Ya'la said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Ya'qub ibn Zayd ibn Talhah, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, and he mentioned the hadith. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to them about the nations. He said: The community of Musa, peace be upon him, split into seventy-one creeds, seventy of them in the Fire and one in Paradise; the community of Isa, peace be upon him, split into seventy-two sects, seventy-one of them in the Fire and one in Paradise; and my community exceeds both sects together by a creed: seventy-two in the Fire and one in Paradise. They said: Who are they, O Messenger of Allah? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The congregation. Ya'qub ibn Zayd said: Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, when he narrated this hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), would recite Qur'an with it: And of the people of Musa there is a community who guide by truth and act justly by it. Then he mentioned the community of Isa, peace be upon him, and said: Had the People of the Book believed and been God-fearing We would have expiated their sins. Then he mentioned our community and said: And of those We created there is a community who guide by truth and act justly by it."
"3553","Wasil ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Layth, from Sa'id ibn Amir, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: In my community are over seventy callers, all calling to the Fire; if I wished I would inform you of their fathers and their tribes."
"3554","Chapter: Warning against innovations. Ishaq said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid informed us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two classes of my community shall not enter Paradise: the Qadariyyah and the Murji'ah. I say: In it is a break."
"3555","Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid informed us, Sulayman ibn Ja'far al-Asadi narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Abi Layla, from his father, from his grandfather Abu Layla, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Two classes of my community shall not come to the Hawd: the Qadariyyah and the Murji'ah."
"3556","Ishaq said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid informed us, Habib ibn Amr al-Ansari narrated to me, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A caller will call on the Day of Resurrection: Let the adversaries of Allah Almighty stand; they are the Qadariyyah."
"3557","Abu Ya'la said: Musa narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd Allah al-Marwazi narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, with this."
"3558","Ishaq said: Sulayman ibn Harb informed us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abu Suwayd, from al-Hasan, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When the delegation of Basrah came to Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, among them al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, he dismissed them and detained him, then said: Do you know why I detained you? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) warned us against every eloquent hypocrite, and I feared you were of them, though I hope you are not of them; finish your estate and join your family. Hammad said: Maymun al-Kurdi said, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, the like. I say: The hadith of Abu Uthman was brought by Ahmad."
"3559","Musaddad said: Hafs narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Malik ibn al-Harith, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Moderation in the Sunnah is better than striving in innovation."
"3560","Abd al-Mu'min Abu Ubaydah narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Abi Mahdi narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: No year comes upon people except they innovate therein a bid'ah and cause a sunnah to die therein, until bid'ahs live and sunnahs die."
"3561","Ibn Abi Umar said: Hisham ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abu Rafi' narrated to us, from Salih ibn Jubayr, and he said: Ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, stood over people, one narrating stories to another, and said: By Allah, you have openly surpassed the Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and you have innovated an innovation unjustly. Follow and do not innovate; by Allah, if you follow you have preceded a clear precedence, and if you innovate you have wronged a distant wrong, or he said: You have gone far astray. The doubt is from Ibn Abi Umar."
"3562","Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Abu Ubaydah al-Haddad narrated to us, from Awf, from Sa'id ibn Khuthaym, from a shaykh of the people of Sham, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) exhorted us with an exhortation, and one said: O Messenger of Allah, as if this is the exhortation of a farewell one. What do you enjoin upon us? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I enjoin upon you to fear Allah Almighty, hold to my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the guided rightly-guided caliphs; bite upon them with the molars. Even if an Abyssinian slave is appointed over you, listen to him and obey; and every innovation is misguidance."
"3563","Abu Ya'la said: al-Hasan ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Awf, with it."
"3564","Ishaq said: Rawh ibn Ubadah informed us, from Husayn al-Mu'allim, from Abd Allah ibn Buraydah, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, gathered people for the arrival of the delegation, and said to Zayd ibn Arqam: Look at the Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and admit them first of people, then the generation after them. They entered and lined before him. They looked and there was a bulky man wearing a patched cloak of striped cloths. Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, gestured to him and he came; Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Eh, three times. The man said: Eh, three times. Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Uff, stand. He stood and looked, and there was al-Ash'ari, a light-bodied short stout man. He gestured to him and he came; Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Eh. Al-Ash'ari said: Eh. Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Eh. He said: O Commander of the Faithful, ask and open a discourse and we will narrate to you. Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Uff, stand; a shepherd of sheep will not benefit you. He looked and there was a fair light-bodied man. He gestured to him and he came; Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Eh. He leapt, praised Allah Almighty, lauded Him and exhorted him by Allah. Then he said: You were entrusted with the affair of this community, so fear Allah Almighty in what you were entrusted of this community and your subjects, in yourself especially; you will be reckoned and asked about what you were entrusted; you are a trustee, and you must render your trust, and be given your reward according to your deed. Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: No man has told me truth since I was made caliph except you. Who are you? He said: I am al-Rabi' ibn Ziyad. He said: Brother of al-Muhajir ibn Ziyad? He said: Yes. Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, equipped an army and appointed al-Ash'ari over them, then said: Look at Rabi' ibn Ziyad; if he is truthful in what he said, he has aid in this affair, so employ him. Then let not ten days pass except you inspect his work and write to me of his conduct in his work, as if I employed him myself. Then Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Our Prophet enjoined upon us and said: What I fear most for you after me is an eloquent hypocrite."
"3565","Al-Harith said: Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: There will be people who deny the Dajjal, deny the rising of the sun from its west, deny the punishment of the grave, and deny a people exiting the Fire after being scorched."
"3566","Ishaq said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid informed us, Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, one who heard Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, say, narrated to me: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not fear for you after me a believing certain one, nor an open disbeliever; as for the certain believer, his faith restrains him, and as for the open one, by his disbelief. But I fear for you after me a scholar of tongue, ignorant of heart, saying what you know and doing what you deny."
"3567","Ghassan al-Kufi Abu Bishr al-Asadi informed us, companion of Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash: Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Farwah narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: A man in a circle in Madinah said: Which of you will narrate to me a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: I; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I do not fear for my community a believer nor a disbeliever; as for the believer his faith prevents him, and as for the disbeliever his disbelief prevents him. But a man between them recites the Qur'an until when fluent in it he interprets it other than its interpretation, saying what you know and doing what you deny, so he strays and leads astray. I say: I think Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Madani mentioned in the first narration is Ishaq mentioned in the second, and Baqiyyah only concealed him for his weakness."
"3568","Jarir informed us, from Amr ibn Qays al-Mula'i, from his father, from Umayyah ibn Yazid al-Shami, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever innovates in Islam an innovation, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels and all people; neither sarf nor adl is accepted from him. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the innovation? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills a soul without a soul, or mutilates a mutilation without retaliation, or innovates a bid'ah without sunnah. He said: Adl is ransom and sarf is repentance. Its chain is hasan but it is mursal or mu'dal."
"3569","Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from a man, from Tawus, he said: Qatadah came to him to sit, and he said to him: If you sit I will stand. They said: O Abu Muhammad, he is a jurist. He said: Iblis is more understanding than him, when he said: My Lord, because You led me astray. I say: He points thereby to what Qatadah was accused of regarding the decree."
"3570","Abu Ya'la said: al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Dinar narrated to us, from al-Khasib ibn Jahdar, from Rashid ibn Sa'd, from Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing worshipped under the sky's shade is more hateful to Allah Almighty than followed desire."
"3571","Chapter: Rebuke against the seat of the Khawarij and deviants. al-Harith said: Ahmad ibn Yazid narrated to us, Hisham ibn Yazid al-Sa'di narrated to us, from Nahshal ibn Sa'id, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, he said: Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Nafi', bring me near the path of the pilgrims. That was after his sight weakened. He did, and he looked at the companions of litters and said: May Allah have mercy on you, how favored you are. Then he looked at the companions of black sacks with men upon them and said: You are the pilgrims; perhaps I shall not meet you after this year of mine. Hear from me a hadith I narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of our qiblah are believers; nothing removes them from faith except the door by which they entered into it."
"3572","Musaddad said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, stood and said: O people, there will be a people of this community who deny stoning, deny the Dajjal, deny the rising of the sun from its west, deny the punishment of the grave, deny intercession, and deny a people exiting the Fire after being scorched."
"3573","Abu Bakr said: Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated to us, Ash'ath narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd the like, and added: And they deny the decree, and deny the Hawd; and he did not mention the Dajjal nor the rising of the sun nor the punishment of the grave."
"3574","Abu Ya'la said: Hudbah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, like the first except the rising of the sun and the punishment of the grave."
"3575","Abu Bakr and Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Awwam ibn Hawshab narrated to us, Talhah ibn Nafi' Abu Sufyan narrated to me, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A man passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and they spoke of him and praised him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will kill him? Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I. He went and found him standing praying, having drawn a line upon himself. Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, returned and did not kill him when he saw him in that state. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will kill him? Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I. He went and saw him standing praying in his line, and returned and did not kill him. The Messenger of Allah said: Who will kill him? Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You, and I do not see you will reach him. He said: He went and found him gone."
"3576","Abu Ya'la said: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, with this."
"3577","Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Ya'qub ibn Zayd ibn Talhah, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A man with harm against the enemy and striving was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I do not know this. They said: Yes, his description is such and such. He said: I do not know him. While we were so, the man appeared. They said: This is he, O Messenger of Allah. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I did not know this; he is the first horn I have seen in my community; in him is a touch of Satan. When the man drew near he greeted and they returned the greeting. He said to him: I adjure you by Allah, did you speak to yourself when you appeared to us that none in the company is better? He said: O Allah, yes. He said: He entered the mosque and prayed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Bakr: Stand and kill him. Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, entered and found him standing praying. Abu Bakr said to himself: Prayer has sanctity and right; had I sought the Messenger of Allah's permission. He came to him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Did you kill him? He, may Allah be pleased with him, said: No; I saw him standing praying, and saw for prayer sanctity and right; if you wish I kill him I will kill him. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are not his man. Go, O Umar, and kill him. Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, entered the mosque and there he was prostrating. He waited long, then Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said to himself: Prostration has right; had I sought the Messenger of Allah's permission, for one better than me sought his permission. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: Did you kill him? He, may Allah be pleased with him, said: No; I saw him prostrating, and saw for prostration right; if you wish I kill him I will kill him? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are not his man. Stand, O Ali, you are his man if you find him. He arrived and found him exited from the mosque. He returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: Did you kill him? He said: No. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had he been killed, no two men of my community would have differed until the Dajjal. This is a strange hadith, and Abu Ma'shar has weakness in him."
"3578","It has another path brought by al-Bazzar, from Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sharik, my father narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until a man of good appearance came; they mentioned good of his affair. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I see on his face a touch of the Fire. When he ended and greeted, he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah, I think he said: Did you say to yourself that you are the best of the company? He said: Yes. When he left, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: His horn and his companions have appeared; among them. Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Shall I not kill him, O Messenger of Allah? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes, and he mentioned the hadith similar to what preceded in brief. Its end: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, went and did not find him, and he mentioned what is after. Al-Bazzar said: We do not know it narrated from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, except from this face; Sharik alone narrated it. I say: He was opposed therein as preceded, for it was said from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him; and it was narrated from other than the hadith of Sharik as you see, with another chain to Anas ibn Malik. In the chapter is from Abu Bakrah, may Allah be pleased with him, with Ahmad and others."
"3579","Chapter: Rejection. Abd said: Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Imran ibn Zayd al-Tha'labi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Tamim narrated to me, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There will be at the end of time a people called al-Rafidah; they reject Islam and cast it off. Fight them, for they are polytheists."
"3580","Abu Ya'la said: Zuhayr narrated to us, Hashim narrated to us, with this."
"3581","Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, Abu Idris narrated to us, from Abu al-Jahhaf Dawud ibn Abi Awf, from Muhammad ibn Amr al-Hashimi, from Zaynab bint Ali, from Fatimah bint Muhammad, may Allah's blessings be upon him and His pleasure upon them, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: This is in Paradise; and among his partisans are a people who display Islam then reject it; they have a nickname, called al-Rafidah. Whoever meets them, let him know they are polytheists."
"3582","Chapter: Abandoning takfir of the people of the qiblah. The hadith of Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, in the chapter of the Khawarij will come if Allah Almighty wills. al-Harith said: Isma'il ibn Abd al-Karim narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Aqil narrated to us, from his father, from Wahb, meaning Ibn Munabbih, he said: I asked Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him: Are there among those who pray tyrants? He said: No. I asked him: Is among them a polytheist? He said: No."
"3583","Abu Ya'la said: Ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, he said: I asked Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, while he was residing in Makkah, settled among Banu Fihr, and a man asked him: Did you call anyone of the people of the qiblah a polytheist? He said: Allah forbid, and he was alarmed at that. I said: Did you call anyone of them a disbeliever? He said: No. Sahih mawquf."
"3584","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Umar ibn Yunus narrated to us, Ikrimah narrated to us, Yazid al-Raqashi narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I said to him: O Abu Hamzah, people testify against us with disbelief and polytheism? Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Those are the worst of creation."
"3585","Musaddad said: Isma'il narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Zayd, from Ja'far al-Abdi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to the swearers of my community who say: So-and-so in Paradise, so-and-so in the Fire."
"3586","Mu'tamir narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, with it."
"3587","al-Harith ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Amir al-Ahwal, from Fitr ibn Khalifah, from Abu Bishr Ja'far ibn Abi Wahshiyyah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty says: Whoever swears upon My servant, I admit My servant to Paradise and admit him to the Fire."
"3588","Chapter: Whispering. Ishaq said: Amr ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi informed us, Umar ibn Dharr narrated to us, from his father, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: O Messenger of Allah, by the One who sent you with truth, a thing presents itself in my breast, and I would love to be charred coal. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Praise be to Allah who has despaired Satan from being worshipped in this land of yours again; but he is content with the belittled of your deeds. I say: Abu Dawud and al-Nasa'i narrated it from the hadith of Dharr, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned part of it, and added: Praise be to Allah who returned his plot to whispering. The first is disconnected."
"3589","Abu Ya'la said: Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Mu'tamir narrated to us, he said: I heard Layth narrating from Shahr ibn Hawshab, he said: A man said to A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her: One of us speaks to himself a thing, if he uttered it his Hereafter would go, and if it appeared he would be killed. She said: She magnified Allah three times, then said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about it, and he magnified three times, then said: Only the believer is tested."
"3590","al-Harith said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Salih, that is al-Murri, narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A man stood to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in my breast is a thing; if I revealed it I would perish. Am I perishing? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No; Allah Almighty has overlooked for my community what their souls speak, as long as they do not speak or act."
"3591","Chapter: Dislike of self-praise. Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Abu Qatan narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: A man said with Abd Allah: I am a believer. Abd Allah said to him: Then say: I am in Paradise. He said: I believed in Allah, His angels, His Books and His messengers."
"3592","Musaddad said: Abd Allah ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Kurayz, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: What I fear most for you is a man's admiration of his opinion; whoever says: I am a scholar is ignorant, and whoever says: I am in Paradise is in the Fire."
"3593","al-Harith said: Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Whoever claims he is a believer is a disbeliever, whoever claims he is in Paradise is in the Fire, and whoever claims he is a scholar is ignorant. He said: A man disputed him, saying: If you take authority, we have Paradise. He said: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever claims he is in Paradise is in the Fire."
"3594","Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us, Mu'arik ibn Abbad al-Qaysi narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man's faith is not complete until he makes exception in all his speech, or he said: In his talk."
"3595","Chapter: Denial of one who believes in return in this world. Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to me, from Amr ibn al-Asamm, he said: I said to al-Hasan ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both: This Shi'ah claims Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, will be sent? He said: They lied; those are not Shi'ah. Had he been sent, we would not have married his wives nor divided his inheritance."
"3596","Chapter: Pardon for what is below polytheism. Abu Ya'la and al-Bazzar together said: Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Suhayl ibn Abi Hazm narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomever Allah Almighty promised reward upon a deed, He will fulfill it to him; and whomever He promised punishment upon a deed, He has choice therein. Al-Bazzar said: Suhayl is not followed in his hadith."
"3597","Chapter: The greatness of Allah and His attributes. Ishaq said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hakam ibn Aban informed us, my father narrated to me, from Ikrimah, regarding His Almighty saying: I shall come to them from before them and from behind them and from their right and from their left. He said: Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said: He could not say: From above them; he knew Allah Almighty is above them."
"3598","Bishr ibn Umar al-Zahrani informed us, he said: I heard more than one of the exegetes say: The Most Merciful rose over the Throne, meaning He ascended."
"3599","Abdah ibn Sulayman informed us, Isma'il ibn Rafi' narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from a man of the Ansar, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us while among a group of his Companions. He said: When Allah Blessed and Almighty created the Trumpet, He gave it to Israfil; he holds it upon his mouth, gazing toward the Throne, waiting until commanded. He mentioned the hadith, and said therein: Then Allah Almighty will place His Throne where He wills of the earth; eight will bear His Throne that day, today four: their feet upon the lowest tracts of the earth, the earths and heavens upon their rumps, the Throne upon their shoulders. They have a humming with glorification; their glorification is to say: Glory to the King, Lord of dominion; glory to the Lord of the Throne, Lord of might; glory to the Living who does not die; glory to Him who causes creatures to die and does not die. Most Glorious, Most Holy, Lord of angels and spirit. Holy, holy; glory to my Lord the Most High; glory to the Lord of dominion, might, pride and greatness. Glory to Him forever. This chain is weak."
"3600","Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid informed us, Bahir ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: Some Jews came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: We ask you about three things known only to a prophet: Inform us about the bearers of the Throne, who are they? And about the fluid of man and the fluid of woman? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for the bearers of the Throne, vermin bear it by their horns, and the sweat in the sun is of their sweat; the fluid of man is white thick, and the fluid of woman is yellow thin. He mentioned the third, and they said: We testify you are a prophet; so we find it in the Torah."
